他说，嘿，我把眼镜落在下面某处了。

299
00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:51.220
Crossing through, beep, beep.
借过一下，哔哔。

300
00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:52.720
He says, beep, beep.
他说，哔哔。

301
00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:55.160
Then she throws it, and he goes, ow.
然后她扔了过去，他就说，哎哟。

302
00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:56.640
And she says, I didn't see you.
她说，我没看见你。

303
00:14:56.740 --> 00:14:58.040
You should have yelled crossing.
你应该喊一声‘过马路了’。

304
00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:00.460
And Toby's like, I'm sorry.
托比就说，抱歉。

305
00:15:00.680 --> 00:15:01.420
And I'm like, oh, my.
我就想，天哪。

306
00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:02.300
He did.
他确实说了。

307
00:15:02.740 --> 00:15:03.760
He literally said.
他真的说了。

308
00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:04.180
He mumbled it.
他嘟囔着说的。

309
00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:05.760
He Toby'd it, though.
不过他那样子确实很‘托比’。

310
00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:09.480
He, like, swallowed it while he was, I'm crossing, beep, beep.
他就像是把话吞进肚子里，一边走一边说，我过马路了，哔哔，哔哔。

311
00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:10.200
Like, come on.
拜托。

312
00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:11.160
I heard the beep, beep.
我听到了哔哔声。

313
00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:13.920
And I went back, and I was like, he totally said it.
我回去之后就说，他绝对说了。

314
00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:17.580
If you're playing golf, you don't go, no, four, beep, beep.
如果你在打高尔夫，你不会说，不，小心，哔哔，哔哔。

315
00:15:18.320 --> 00:15:19.640
You're like, four.
你会直接喊，小心。

316
00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:21.620
You know what I'm saying?
你明白我的意思吗？

317
00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:23.000
I know, but I thought the beep, beep.
我明白，但我以为那个哔哔声……

318
00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.420
Make your presence known, Toby.
让别人注意到你啊，托比。

319
00:15:24.580 --> 00:15:24.720
OK.
好吧。

320
00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:25.340
All right.
行吧。

321
00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:28.320
But we got a fan question from Ryan S.
我们收到了来自马萨诸塞州瑞安·S的一位粉丝提问。

322
00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:34.100
in Massachusetts who said, in the cold open, when Pam throws her plane, is that CGI special effects?
他说，在开场戏里，帕姆扔纸飞机的时候，那是CGI特效吗？

323
00:15:34.100 --> 00:15:38.460
Or did Jenna really have to practice throwing a paper plane right into Paul's eye?
还是说珍娜真的得练习把纸飞机扔进保罗的眼睛里？

324
00:15:39.840 --> 00:15:46.540
Well, Ryan, I really did throw a paper airplane, but the part where it hit Toby was visual effects.
嗯，瑞安，我确实扔了纸飞机，但击中托比的那部分是视觉特效。

325
00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:47.700
So here's what we did.
我们是这样做的。

326
00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:50.280
This was three different shots that we put all together.
这是三个不同的镜头拼在一起的。

327
00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:53.780
So the first thing we did was an angle on me throwing a plane.
首先，我们拍了我扔飞机的角度。

328
00:15:54.900 --> 00:16:03.260
Then we shot a paper airplane flying through the air that was thrown by a professional, not by me, toward nothing.
然后我们拍了一个纸飞机在空中飞行的镜头，是由专业人士扔的，不是我，而且是朝着空气扔的。

329
00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:05.120
Toby was not standing there.
当时托比并没有站在那里。

330
00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:12.820
And then we filmed Toby reacting as if he had gotten hit with a paper airplane that he was not hit with.
接着我们拍了托比的反应，就好像他被纸飞机击中了一样，但他其实并没有被击中。

331
00:16:12.960 --> 00:16:17.840
And then we combine all the shots together, and it makes it look like he's getting hit in the eye.
最后我们把所有镜头合在一起，看起来就像他被击中了眼睛一样。

332
00:16:18.280 --> 00:16:19.120
Did that make sense?
这样说清楚了吗？

333
00:16:19.340 --> 00:16:20.460
It did make sense.
说清楚了。

334
00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:27.420
You know, Halstead shared with us that even though it seems like a fairly simple moment, it took two full days to shoot this.
你知道吗，霍尔斯特德告诉我们，虽然这看起来是一个相当简单的瞬间，但拍这个镜头花了两整天。

335
00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:28.860
So crazy.
太疯狂了。

336
00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:29.780
Crazy.
疯狂。

337
00:16:30.520 --> 00:16:36.720
And he also went on to say, I think Pam flying a plane into Toby's eye was one of the first scenes shot.
他还接着说，我觉得帕姆把飞机扔进托比眼睛里的戏是第一批拍摄的场景之一。

338
00:16:36.900 --> 00:16:42.000
And I remember Jenna saying, I think this is incredibly broad, which let's face it, it's true.
我记得珍娜当时说，我觉得这太夸张了，说实话，确实如此。

339
00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:55.340
Well, because originally, originally, they gave Paul an airplane to like hold between his fingers as if it was stabbing him in the eye.
因为最初，最初他们给了保罗一个纸飞机，让他夹在手指间，好像飞机刺进了他的眼睛一样。

340
00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:56.460
I remember that.
我记得那个。

341
00:16:56.720 --> 00:17:00.100
And I was like, guys, that looks ridiculously broad.
我就说，伙计们，这看起来太荒谬、太夸张了。

342
00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:02.060
I think it became a blooper moment.
我觉得那成了个笑场片段。

343
00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:02.920
It did.
确实是。

344
00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:06.100
And then they decided to take that part out.
然后他们决定把那部分删掉。

345
00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:08.240
You just see it hits him and falls on the ground.
你现在只能看到它击中他然后掉在地上。

346
00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:12.580
Well, we will share the bloopers in our stories, but here it is for you to hear.
我们会把笑场片段分享在我们的快拍里，现在先放给你们听听。

347
00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:17.040
Oh, how's it look?
噢，看起来怎么样？

348
00:17:17.420 --> 00:17:18.300
What should he do?
他该怎么办？

349
00:17:18.460 --> 00:17:20.200
It looks ridiculously broad.
看起来荒谬得太夸张了。

350
00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:28.140
And we are laughing so hard because it did.
我们当时笑得不行，因为确实太搞笑了。

351
00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:35.180
He had a cartoonish like plane like stuck to his like head to look like it's coming out his eye.
他头上粘了个卡通飞机，看起来就像是从他眼睛里长出来的一样。

352
00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:36.280
It looked ridiculous.
看起来太荒唐了。

353
00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:39.240
Yes, thankfully, we changed it.
是啊，谢天谢地，我们改掉了。

354
00:17:39.500 --> 00:17:44.860
But I guess after the paper airplane hits Toby and lands on the ground, Pam is like, so is this my spot?
但我想在纸飞机击中托比并落在地上后，帕姆大概是想说，这是我的位置吗？

355
00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:46.440
And she's out of the conteSt.
然后她就被淘汰了。

356
00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:49.540
She's like, yeah, yeah, yeah, your eye.
她大概是说，是啊是啊，你的眼睛。

357
00:17:49.680 --> 00:17:50.620
Is this where I landed?
这是我落下的地方吗？

358
00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:53.080
Well, now they're down to an elite eight.
好吧，现在只剩下八强了。

359
00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:54.440
Well, seven and Toby.
准确说是七个人加上托比。

360
00:17:55.000 --> 00:18:00.320
I want to say Nellie's commentary, her little bits she does are so funny throughout the whole thing.
我想说奈莉的解说，她在整个过程中穿插的小段子真是太搞笑了。

361
00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:03.420
I loved her little outfit, her little referee outfit.
我很喜欢她那身小行头，她那身小裁判服。

362
00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:03.900
I know.
我知道。

363
00:18:04.340 --> 00:18:05.260
It's looking very cute.
看起来非常可爱。

364
00:18:05.260 --> 00:18:05.960
It's that choice.
这就是那个选择。

365
00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:07.720
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

366
00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:09.380
This would be a special project.
这会是一个特别项目。

367
00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:10.620
This is her domain.
这是她的地盘。

368
00:18:11.080 --> 00:18:11.340
Yes.
没错。

369
00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:14.260
Now we're going to start Andy's storyline.
现在我们要开始安迪的故事线了。

370
00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:17.320
And I have to do some applause for Ed HelMs.
我得为艾德·赫尔姆斯鼓鼓掌。

371
00:18:17.460 --> 00:18:20.640
He was so hilarious in this episode.
他在这一集里太搞笑了。

372
00:18:20.800 --> 00:18:22.840
I really enjoyed his performance.
我真的很享受他的表演。

373
00:18:23.480 --> 00:18:26.320
What's happening is he's running lines with Daryl.
剧情是他正在和达里尔对台词。

374
00:18:26.320 --> 00:18:31.780
And, you know, he's going way too big and way too broad for whatever this script is.
你知道，无论这剧本写的是什么，他演得都太夸张、太放飞自我了。

375
00:18:32.240 --> 00:18:34.780
Daryl's saying things like, there's no exclamation point.
达里尔说，这里没有感叹号。

376
00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:36.220
It's not acidic.
这又不是酸性的。

377
00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:38.100
Like the things he's talking about.
就像他说的那些东西一样。

378
00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:48.740
And this is when we find out that last week, Andy got an agent and this week, a movie, the HRPDC Chemical Handling Protocols Industrial.
这时我们才知道，上周安迪找了个经纪人，这周就接了一部电影，叫《HRPDC化学品处理规程工业宣传片》。

379
00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:50.300
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

380
00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:51.520
Andy's like, you never know.
安迪说，谁知道呢。

381
00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:54.640
Could be seen by Brad Pitt's brother.
没准会被布拉德·皮特的兄弟看到。

382
00:18:54.640 --> 00:18:57.320
And then next thing I know, I'm in Moneyballs, too.
然后下一秒我就能去演《点球成金2》了。

383
00:18:58.380 --> 00:19:02.620
So, you know, my first acting job was in industrial, just like Andy.
所以，你知道，我的第一份表演工作也是工业宣传片，和安迪一样。

384
00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:07.220
My first paid acting job in Los Angeles where I had lines.
我在洛杉矶的第一份有台词的带薪表演工作。

385
00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:16.600
You know, my first acting job was as an extra on the Jurassic Park ride at Universal Studios where I was doused with water for about 12 hours.
你知道，我的第一份表演工作是在环球影城的侏罗纪公园游乐设施里当群演，我被水浇了大概12个小时。

386
00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:17.420
Oh, gosh.
天哪。

387
00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:24.960
But my first speaking role was in an industrial for the UCLA medical facility.
但我第一个有台词的角色是在加州大学洛杉矶分校医疗中心的一个工业宣传片里。

388
00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:32.960
And it was a sex education video for patients upon their release from the hospital.
那是一个给患者出院时看的性教育视频。

389
00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:35.400
What kind of things did you have to say?
你得说些什么内容？

390
00:19:35.640 --> 00:19:38.900
I was a girl and I was going on a date.
我演一个要去约会的女孩。

391
00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:45.960
And my sister says to me as I'm getting ready to leave, she says, well, have fun on your date.
我准备出门时，我姐姐对我说，玩得开心点。

392
00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:47.400
I hope you have protection.
希望你带了防护措施。

393
00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:49.800
And I say, protection?
我说，防护措施？

394
00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:50.640
What?
什么？

395
00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:51.940
Protection from what?
防什么？

396
00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:56.780
And she says, from pregnancy and sexually transmitted diseases.
她说，防止怀孕和性传播疾病。

397
00:19:56.880 --> 00:19:57.900
Come here.
过来。

398
00:19:58.100 --> 00:19:59.500
And she's a nurse.
而且她演的是个护士。

399
00:19:59.660 --> 00:20:01.020
She's dressed like a nurse.
她穿着护士服。

400
00:20:01.020 --> 00:20:06.060
And she talks about sexually transmitted diseases and various diseases.
她在那儿大谈特谈性传播疾病和各种疾病。

401
00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:08.640
I mostly listen very earnestly.
我通常听得非常认真。

402
00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:16.020
And then at the end, I say something along the lines of, well, now I feel prepared for my date.
然后在最后，我会说些类似“嗯，现在我觉得为约会做好准备了”之类的话。

403
00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:18.120
Like, what is the first date?
比如，什么是第一次约会？

404
00:20:19.340 --> 00:20:20.620
Has high stakes.
赌注很高。

405
00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:21.170
What is happening?
到底发生了什么？

406
00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:21.720
I don't know.
我不知道。

407
00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:24.560
I'm also like, it's just coffee.
我也会想，这不过就是喝杯咖啡而已。

408
00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:26.580
Like, it's going to be fine.
没事的，会很顺利的。

409
00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:29.040
And were you like, Andy?
那你当时是安迪吗？

410
00:20:29.220 --> 00:20:30.820
Were you like, this is my moment?
你当时是不是觉得，这就是我的高光时刻？

411
00:20:32.140 --> 00:20:33.520
I have arrived.
我终于熬出头了。

412
00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:35.620
I was very prepared.
我准备得非常充分。

413
00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:37.340
I knew all my lines.
我背熟了所有的台词。

414
00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:40.260
I knew how I was going to react to all of the diseases.
我知道该怎么应对所有那些疾病相关的台词。

415
00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:42.540
I was paid $100.
我拿到了100美元的报酬。

416
00:20:43.080 --> 00:20:44.740
And I did my own hair and makeup.
而且我自己做了发型和化妆。

417
00:20:45.860 --> 00:20:47.660
Well, very similar to Andy.
嗯，和安迪的情况非常像。

418
00:20:48.360 --> 00:20:50.000
He's going to do his own hair and makeup.
他也要自己做发型和化妆。

419
00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:51.180
It's in a deleted scene.
这在删减片段里。

420
00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:52.200
We'll get to it.
我们待会儿会讲到。

421
00:20:52.300 --> 00:20:53.080
I'm going to share it.
我会分享出来的。

422
00:20:53.260 --> 00:21:00.480
But you know, I remember one of my first big auditions that I was so excited about
但你知道，我记得我第一次参加的大型试镜之一，当时我非常兴奋，

423
00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:07.100
was an industrial for Ford motor cars where I would be in a lab coat.
那是为福特汽车拍的一部工业宣传片，我得穿上实验服。

424
00:21:07.400 --> 00:21:11.500
The audition, they actually had us read off a teleprompter because they wanted to see
试镜时，他们实际上让我们对着提词器念，因为他们想看看

425
00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:14.340
if you could do that because there was going to be a lot of that.
你能不能做到，因为之后会有很多这样的内容。

426
00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:20.560
And I talked about, like, the new engine and the words coming out of my mouth.
我当时在谈论新引擎什么的，那些词从我嘴里说出来，

427
00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:22.000
I didn't even understand them.
我自己甚至都听不懂。

428
00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:23.800
And I'm sure no one believed it.
我敢肯定没人会相信我。

429
00:21:23.900 --> 00:21:29.140
I was saying things like, you know, it has twin independent variable camshaft timing.
我当时在说些什么“双独立可变凸轮轴正时”之类的词。

430
00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:32.720
And I was like, I did not get the part, you guys.
我当时就想，伙计们，我没拿到那个角色。

431
00:21:32.900 --> 00:21:33.740
I did not get it.
我没选上。

432
00:21:34.420 --> 00:21:37.300
But it cracked me up that this was Andy's storyline.
但安迪的这条故事线让我笑喷了。

433
00:21:37.300 --> 00:21:39.940
And I love that Halstead shared this.
我很喜欢霍尔斯特德分享的这些。

434
00:21:40.120 --> 00:21:42.580
He said, we knew at the beginning of many actors' careers,
他说，我们都知道在许多演员职业生涯的初期，

435
00:21:42.660 --> 00:21:46.420
they could get cast in commercials or corporate industrial filMs.
他们可能会被选中去拍广告或企业工业宣传片。

436
00:21:46.620 --> 00:21:51.320
We thought it would be really funny to see Andy get cast in an industrial film,
我们觉得让安迪去拍一部工业宣传片会非常有趣，

437
00:21:51.440 --> 00:21:53.520
which was super dry and boring,
那片子枯燥乏味到了极点，

438
00:21:53.720 --> 00:21:57.320
but that Andy would treat it as if it was an Oscar-winning performance.
但安迪却把它当成奥斯卡获奖级别的表演来对待。

439
00:21:57.320 --> 00:21:59.360
I mean, we all did.
我是说，我们当时都是这样。

440
00:21:59.600 --> 00:22:00.720
This is all true.
这全都是真的。

441
00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:04.980
Oh, it took me right back to that Ford industrial.
噢，这让我瞬间回到了拍那部福特宣传片的时候。

442
00:22:05.720 --> 00:22:12.980
Well, I guess all of this is just to say that this is a very accurate depiction of a new actor getting their first role.
好吧，我想这一切只是为了说明，这非常真实地描绘了一个新演员拿到第一个角色时的样子。

443
00:22:13.300 --> 00:22:13.820
Yes.
没错。

444
00:22:14.120 --> 00:22:14.640
Well done.
干得好。

445
00:22:15.160 --> 00:22:15.900
Oh, boy.
天哪。

446
00:22:16.040 --> 00:22:18.220
Now we're going to move into the Jim and Pam storyline.
现在我们要进入吉姆和帕姆的故事线了。

447
00:22:18.760 --> 00:22:19.780
Oh, gosh.
噢，天哪。

448
00:22:20.160 --> 00:22:21.720
This made me cringe.
这让我看得尴尬症都犯了。

449
00:22:21.720 --> 00:22:30.660
There were times where I was really cringing because it felt like this forced exercise that they were really trying to get behind.
有好几次我真的觉得很尴尬，因为这感觉就像是一种他们极力想要配合的强迫性练习。

450
00:22:31.360 --> 00:22:32.240
But, man.
但是，天呐。

451
00:22:32.860 --> 00:22:37.140
Pam is really difficult in this episode, isn't she?
这一集里的帕姆真的很让人头疼，不是吗？

452
00:22:37.420 --> 00:22:41.180
Like, I feel like Jim is being a better team player here.
我觉得吉姆在这方面表现得更像个团队合作者。

453
00:22:41.320 --> 00:22:44.480
And Pam is, you can see how closed off she is.
而帕姆，你能看出她有多封闭自己。

454
00:22:44.580 --> 00:22:47.480
I mean, later she's going to have a talking head about it.
我是说，稍后她会有一个单独的访谈片段来谈论这件事。

455
00:22:47.480 --> 00:22:50.520
Her truth is she's not ready to forgive him.
她的真实想法是她还没准备好原谅他。

456
00:22:50.720 --> 00:22:51.540
That's her truth.
这就是她的真实想法。

457
00:22:51.820 --> 00:22:56.760
And she's doing these exercises, and it seems like he's really trying.
她在做这些练习，而且看起来他真的很努力。

458
00:22:57.080 --> 00:23:01.960
So, yeah, you do feel her bumping up against that effort, you know?
所以，没错，你能感觉到她在抵触这种努力，你懂吗？

459
00:23:02.140 --> 00:23:10.660
But have you ever been in that situation before where, like, when the other person is finally acknowledging that the situation is shitty and they're trying,
但你有没有经历过那种情况，就是当对方终于承认情况很糟糕并试图做出改变时，

460
00:23:10.660 --> 00:23:15.880
your first response is kind of, like, too little too late, buddy.
你的第一反应却是：太晚了，伙计。

461
00:23:16.440 --> 00:23:18.260
Because you haven't been angry yet.
因为你还没来得及生气呢。

462
00:23:18.360 --> 00:23:20.300
You haven't gotten to be mad yet.
你还没能发泄出你的愤怒。

463
00:23:20.440 --> 00:23:21.980
And so I think that's where Pam is.
所以我认为帕姆现在就是这种状态。

464
00:23:22.100 --> 00:23:23.840
Pam's, like, finally has permission.
帕姆终于得到了许可。

465
00:23:24.440 --> 00:23:25.740
She's being seen.
她被看见了。

466
00:23:25.980 --> 00:23:26.460
Yeah.
没错。

467
00:23:26.460 --> 00:23:28.300
And she needs to start by being mad.
她需要从愤怒开始。

468
00:23:28.660 --> 00:23:28.860
Yeah.
没错。

469
00:23:29.040 --> 00:23:33.440
But the first thing she's going to do is get an apple from the vending machine, and that was scripted.
但她做的第一件事是从自动贩卖机拿了个苹果，那是剧本里写好的。

470
00:23:33.720 --> 00:23:34.660
That was scripted.
那是剧本里写好的。

471
00:23:34.660 --> 00:23:37.880
I noticed that I got an apple, and I was like, that's so weird.
我注意到我拿了个苹果，当时我就想，这太奇怪了。

472
00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:50.680
We almost never got fruit, but it was scripted that Pam was getting an apple, and Jim comes and sees her in the break room, and they're doing this, you know, couples therapy speak.
我们几乎从不拿水果，但剧本里写着帕姆要拿个苹果，然后吉姆过来在休息室看到了她，他们正在用那种夫妻治疗的口吻说话。

473
00:23:51.420 --> 00:23:54.300
Yes, they're expressing how much they appreciate one another.
是的，他们在表达彼此有多么感激对方。

474
00:23:54.820 --> 00:23:59.500
And then they have a joint talking head where we find out that they're doing couples therapy.
然后他们有一个共同的访谈片段，我们发现他们正在进行夫妻治疗。

475
00:23:59.880 --> 00:24:05.000
They want to find every opportunity to acknowledge and appreciate one another's sacrifices.
他们想要寻找每一个机会来认可和感激对方的牺牲。

476
00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:10.700
And also, they have to use the word opportunity for things that they're not super happy about.
而且，他们必须用“机会”这个词来形容那些他们不太乐意的事情。

477
00:24:11.840 --> 00:24:19.400
This made me laugh because I rebrand things like this to my kids, like things my kids maybe don't want to do.
这让我笑了，因为我也经常这样重新包装事情给我的孩子们，比如那些他们可能不想做的事情。

478
00:24:19.520 --> 00:24:20.680
I call them an experiment.
我把它们称为“实验”。

479
00:24:21.460 --> 00:24:26.420
I'll be like, hey, kids, I'm experimenting with a new vegetable for dinner tonight.
我会说，嘿，孩子们，我今晚要实验一种新的蔬菜作为晚餐。

480
00:24:27.400 --> 00:24:35.660
Or I'll be like, hey, as an experiment, I think we're going to have you guys do the dishes every night this week as an experiment.
或者我会说，嘿，作为一项实验，我想这周你们每天晚上都要洗碗，这只是个实验。

481
00:24:35.780 --> 00:24:37.500
But I also do that to myself.
但我对自己也这样做。

482
00:24:37.740 --> 00:24:45.680
I'll be like, I'm experimenting with taking a walk every day, and then I'm going to analyze how that made my body feel at the end of the week.
我会说，我正在实验每天散步，然后到周末我会分析这让我的身体感觉如何。

483
00:24:46.120 --> 00:24:51.180
Somehow, like if I brand it as an experiment, kind of like how they're saying things are opportunities.
不知怎么的，如果我把它包装成一个实验，就像他们把事情称为“机会”一样。

484
00:24:51.780 --> 00:24:52.520
Opportunities, yeah.
机会，没错。

485
00:24:53.040 --> 00:24:53.900
It is funny.
这很有趣。

486
00:24:54.060 --> 00:25:02.380
It's a very, I think, parenting thing to do because I know sometimes if our kids are frustrated with like, oh, we got a new school schedule.
我觉得这是一种很典型的育儿方式，因为我知道有时候如果我们的孩子因为比如，哦，我们拿到了新的学校课程表而感到沮丧。

487
00:25:02.600 --> 00:25:04.020
You know, they're getting their schedules.
你知道，他们拿到了课程表。

488
00:25:04.020 --> 00:25:04.800
It's high school.
那是高中。

489
00:25:05.660 --> 00:25:08.400
And sometimes the classes don't line up the way they want it.
有时候课程安排得不如他们所愿。

490
00:25:08.420 --> 00:25:09.200
And I'm like, well, you know what?
我就说，好吧，你知道吗？

491
00:25:09.280 --> 00:25:10.180
That's information.
那是信息。

492
00:25:10.620 --> 00:25:12.220
You just got some information.
你刚刚得到了一些信息。

493
00:25:12.880 --> 00:25:14.220
So I say that.
所以我总是这么说。

494
00:25:14.220 --> 00:25:21.720
Or if like someone is maybe not like as friendly as they had hoped or, you know, whatever it is at school.
或者如果有人可能不像他们希望的那样友好，或者，你知道，学校里发生的任何事情。

495
00:25:21.860 --> 00:25:24.120
I'm like, well, that's information you just learned.
我会说，好吧，那是你刚刚学到的信息。

496
00:25:24.380 --> 00:25:25.900
So I say information.
所以我说的是信息。

497
00:25:26.540 --> 00:25:33.080
And then it just makes me think of how all these years, all the extra talking heads were called candy bag.
这让我想起这些年来，所有多余的访谈片段都被称为“糖果袋”。

498
00:25:33.360 --> 00:25:34.380
The candy bag.
糖果袋。

499
00:25:34.540 --> 00:25:36.160
You know, we've talked about this, Jenna.
你知道，我们谈过这个，珍娜。

500
00:25:36.300 --> 00:25:38.140
And I was always like, oh, it's the candy bag.
我总是说，哦，那是糖果袋。

501
00:25:38.260 --> 00:25:40.000
And Greg was like, I called it that.
格雷格当时说，我给它起了那个名字。

502
00:25:40.160 --> 00:25:41.880
So maybe you guys wouldn't be annoyed.
这样你们可能就不会觉得烦了。

503
00:25:41.880 --> 00:25:43.180
I thought, what would my kids like?
我想，孩子们会喜欢什么呢？

504
00:25:43.280 --> 00:25:44.200
Oh, a candy bag.
哦，糖果袋。

505
00:25:48.180 --> 00:25:48.860
That's right.
没错。

506
00:25:48.860 --> 00:25:54.680
If it was called the extra work bag, we'd be like, oh, get out the candy bag.
如果叫它额外工作袋，我们肯定会说，哦，把糖果袋拿出来吧。

507
00:25:54.820 --> 00:25:55.740
It's so true.
太对了。

508
00:25:56.020 --> 00:25:57.980
There's fun treats in here for you guys.
这里面有给你们准备的有趣零食。

509
00:25:58.160 --> 00:25:59.840
Sorry, you have to stay another half an hour.
抱歉，你们还得再待半小时。

510
00:26:00.180 --> 00:26:06.940
Well, Warren and Halstead said this storyline was based on the experience of one of the writers who had shared about doing couples therapy.
沃伦和霍尔斯特德说，这个故事情节是基于一位编剧分享的夫妻治疗经历。

511
00:26:07.280 --> 00:26:10.480
This writer helped them come up with all these exercises.
这位编剧帮他们想出了所有这些练习。

512
00:26:11.180 --> 00:26:14.720
Warren said that one particular phrase really tickled him.
沃伦说，有一个特定的短语让他觉得特别好笑。

513
00:26:14.920 --> 00:26:16.760
It was the, I appreciate you.
就是那句，我很欣赏你。

514
00:26:17.240 --> 00:26:22.680
He said this was something he felt like he'd started to see a lot of NBA athletes say in interviews.
他说他觉得这好像是他开始在很多NBA球员的采访中经常听到的话。

515
00:26:22.900 --> 00:26:27.120
And he always felt like it was sort of a subtle code for, I hate this.
而且他总觉得这是一种委婉的暗语，意思是，我讨厌这个。

516
00:26:28.860 --> 00:26:30.200
Or I hate you.
或者我讨厌你。

517
00:26:30.660 --> 00:26:32.440
Oh, I appreciate that question.
哦，我很欣赏这个问题。

518
00:26:32.740 --> 00:26:34.080
I appreciate that.
我很感激这一点。

519
00:26:34.180 --> 00:26:35.880
I appreciate you asking me about that.
我很感谢你问我这个问题。

520
00:26:37.840 --> 00:26:43.520
Well, lady, I have to tell you, when I was looking up this episode, you know, we do all the things.
好吧，女士，我得告诉你，当我查找这一集资料时，你知道的，我们什么都做。

521
00:26:43.520 --> 00:26:44.720
We go back in time.
我们会回顾过去。

522
00:26:44.720 --> 00:26:45.940
We read the shooting draft.
我们会阅读拍摄剧本。

523
00:26:45.940 --> 00:26:47.120
We look at the call sheets.
我们会查看通告单。

524
00:26:47.140 --> 00:26:49.040
And I always check my digital clutter.
我还会检查我的数字杂物。

525
00:26:50.060 --> 00:26:52.720
And what a treasure trove.
简直是个宝库。

526
00:26:53.180 --> 00:26:54.940
I could not believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

527
00:26:55.500 --> 00:26:59.320
Apparently, the week we filmed this, you and I took our cameras.
显然，我们拍摄这一周的时候，你和我带了相机。

528
00:26:59.840 --> 00:27:01.740
I took tons of pictures in the warehouse.
我在仓库里拍了大量的照片。

529
00:27:02.000 --> 00:27:04.940
These are pictures, lady, I have never seen.
这些照片，女士，我从来没见过。

530
00:27:04.940 --> 00:27:06.840
Not even for our book.
连我们的书里都没有。

531
00:27:06.980 --> 00:27:08.840
I found an old email account.
我找到了一个旧邮箱账号。

532
00:27:09.300 --> 00:27:10.380
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

533
00:27:10.640 --> 00:27:11.720
I forgot about.
我都忘了。

534
00:27:12.160 --> 00:27:15.800
And you, I found an email from you to this old email account.
而且，我发现了你发给这个旧邮箱的一封邮件。

535
00:27:15.940 --> 00:27:17.380
And I was like, oh, my gosh.
当时我就想，天哪。

536
00:27:17.800 --> 00:27:19.520
And I was able to get into it.
我成功登录进去了。

537
00:27:19.640 --> 00:27:21.960
And there's all of these photos, lady.
里面全是这些照片，女士。

538
00:27:22.420 --> 00:27:24.380
No, of this episode and more?
不，是这一集的还有其他的吗？

539
00:27:24.580 --> 00:27:26.120
This episode and more.
这一集的还有其他的。

540
00:27:26.280 --> 00:27:30.620
And in particular, you and I were like, oh, we've got to document everything.
特别是，你当时跟我说，哦，我们得把一切都记录下来。

541
00:27:31.320 --> 00:27:32.940
Yes, I remember that.
是的，我记得。

542
00:27:33.140 --> 00:27:38.440
As we were getting to these last kind of six, seven episodes, we started bringing our camera
当我们拍到最后六七集的时候，我们又开始带相机

543
00:27:38.440 --> 00:27:39.180
to work again.
去上班了。

544
00:27:39.300 --> 00:27:39.560
Yes.
是的。

545
00:27:39.680 --> 00:27:41.560
A good camera, like not just our phone.
一台好相机，不仅仅是我们的手机。

546
00:27:41.800 --> 00:27:42.880
So many pictures.
照片太多了。

547
00:27:43.060 --> 00:27:45.000
I have started folders now.
我现在已经开始整理文件夹了。

548
00:27:45.660 --> 00:27:50.360
And also, I found an email from Greg, and I wanted to read it to you.
而且，我还发现了一封格雷格的邮件，我想读给你听。

549
00:27:50.640 --> 00:27:50.880
Okay.
好的。

550
00:27:50.880 --> 00:27:57.000
So this was on February 13th, 2013, 1.31 p.m.
这封邮件是2013年2月13日下午1点31分发的。

551
00:27:57.060 --> 00:27:58.880
You know, I like to know the timestamp.
你知道，我喜欢知道时间戳。

552
00:27:59.520 --> 00:28:00.140
You do.
你确实喜欢。

553
00:28:00.280 --> 00:28:02.000
It goes back to my travel journaling.
这要追溯到我写旅行日记的习惯。

554
00:28:02.920 --> 00:28:05.260
He wrote, hey, brilliant caSt.
他写道，嘿，才华横溢的演员们。

555
00:28:05.580 --> 00:28:10.440
We are thinking about putting together a trip to Scranton on May 1st to take a victory lap,
我们正在考虑在5月1日组织一次斯克兰顿之旅，去进行一次胜利巡游，

556
00:28:10.700 --> 00:28:12.380
promote the last three episodes.
为最后三集做宣传。

557
00:28:12.540 --> 00:28:15.420
And we'd like to shoot a little scene or two for the finale.
而且我们想为大结局拍一两个小场景。

558
00:28:15.700 --> 00:28:19.380
The people who organized the first office convention are excited to do it.
组织过第一次办公室大会的人们对此感到很兴奋。

559
00:28:19.380 --> 00:28:22.300
For those of you who've never been, it's pretty exciting.
对于那些没去过的人来说，那真的很令人激动。

560
00:28:22.680 --> 00:28:26.880
The police force of the city is marshaled to drive us around, and it's a huge deal for
这座城市的警察部队会出动为我们开道，这对当地的每一个人来说

561
00:28:26.880 --> 00:28:28.020
everybody that lives there.
都是一件大事。

562
00:28:28.640 --> 00:28:32.600
Last time, we attracted 5,000 fans from as far away as Ireland.
上次，我们吸引了5000名粉丝，甚至有从爱尔兰远道而来的。

563
00:28:33.140 --> 00:28:36.000
Please let me know if this could be something you could welcome into your schedule.
如果这能安排进你们的日程，请务必告诉我。

564
00:28:37.480 --> 00:28:41.860
Also, side note, I want to save all of your desks together.
另外，顺便提一下，我想把你们所有的办公桌都留下来。

565
00:28:42.100 --> 00:28:46.500
And I think it would make it more special if you wrote a note in the bottom of your desk
我觉得如果你们能在办公桌抽屉底部写上一张便条，

566
00:28:46.500 --> 00:28:46.800
drawer.
会更有纪念意义。

567
00:28:47.240 --> 00:28:48.640
Anybody want to do that?
有人愿意这样做吗？

568
00:28:48.640 --> 00:28:49.960
Not best, Greg.
不太行，格雷格。

569
00:28:50.940 --> 00:28:53.280
So we all wrote in our desk drawers.
所以我们都在办公桌抽屉里写了字。

570
00:28:53.840 --> 00:28:54.280
Yeah.
是啊。

571
00:28:54.720 --> 00:28:56.540
And I don't think Greg got our desks.
而且我觉得格雷格没能拿到我们的桌子。

572
00:28:57.080 --> 00:28:58.480
I don't think he did either.
我觉得他也没拿到。

573
00:28:58.740 --> 00:29:01.420
After all of that, I remember they wouldn't let him have them.
毕竟，我记得他们不让他拿走那些桌子。

574
00:29:01.780 --> 00:29:02.200
Yeah.
是啊。

575
00:29:02.780 --> 00:29:03.820
Which is a real bummer.
这真的很扫兴。

576
00:29:04.100 --> 00:29:06.980
And that trip to Scranton ended up getting pushed till later.
而且那次斯克兰顿之行最终被推迟了。

577
00:29:07.160 --> 00:29:08.680
We didn't film episodes there.
我们没能在那里拍摄剧集。

578
00:29:08.980 --> 00:29:12.540
But I forgot that we signed our desk drawers for Greg.
但我忘了我们还为格雷格在办公桌抽屉上签了名。

579
00:29:12.540 --> 00:29:18.100
Every time we go into our digital clutter and we find these emails from Greg and they're
每当我们翻看数字文档，发现这些来自格雷格的邮件，它们开头总是

580
00:29:18.100 --> 00:29:23.280
say, dear brilliant cast, I get a little choked up because that's how he started all
写着，亲爱的才华横溢的演员们，我都会有点哽咽，因为他给我们的所有邮件

581
00:29:23.280 --> 00:29:29.440
of his emails to us and how he continues to write emails to us to this day.
都是这样开头的，直到今天他写给我们的邮件依然如此。

582
00:29:29.900 --> 00:29:29.960
Yeah.
是啊。

583
00:29:30.820 --> 00:29:33.600
Well, anyway, that was just a little moment back in time.
好吧，总之，那只是过去的一点小插曲。

584
00:29:33.960 --> 00:29:36.380
Well, that made me like very nostalgic.
好吧，这让我感到非常怀旧。

585
00:29:36.820 --> 00:29:37.520
I know.
我知道。

586
00:29:38.320 --> 00:29:39.040
Let's see.
让我看看。

587
00:29:39.160 --> 00:29:39.860
Where are we?
我们讲到哪了？

588
00:29:40.400 --> 00:29:44.920
Oh, Andy is going to announce his new job to the whole bullpen.
哦，安迪要向整个办公室宣布他的新工作了。

589
00:29:44.920 --> 00:29:45.980
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

590
00:29:46.620 --> 00:29:51.800
And he's going to tell Oscar that he's going to use Oscar's recent breakup with the senator
他还要告诉奥斯卡，如果他需要酝酿情绪，他会利用奥斯卡最近和参议员的分手

591
00:29:52.460 --> 00:29:54.700
for inspiration if he needs to get emotional.
作为灵感来源。

592
00:29:54.940 --> 00:29:57.920
And Oscar's like, why don't you just use your own life?
奥斯卡就说，你为什么不直接用你自己的生活呢？

