拜托。

906
00:43:47.730 --> 00:43:47.950
Jeez.
天哪。

907
00:43:48.850 --> 00:43:52.370
Oh, hey, if they interview you for the behind the scenes, talk about how much we laughed on set.
噢，对了，如果他们采访你做幕后花絮，记得提一下我们在片场笑得有多开心。

908
00:43:56.560 --> 00:43:57.820
My hands are really sweaty.
我的手心一直在冒汗。

909
00:43:59.020 --> 00:44:00.520
I think it's because it's so hot.
我想是因为天气太热了。

910
00:44:00.840 --> 00:44:01.980
It's 50 degrees outside.
外面才50度（华氏）。

911
00:44:03.580 --> 00:44:05.480
When my hands sweat, I squeeze ice cubes.
我手心出汗时，就会捏冰块。

912
00:44:05.820 --> 00:44:07.000
It makes them sweat less.
这样能让手少出点汗。

913
00:44:07.180 --> 00:44:07.500
Really?
真的吗？

914
00:44:07.860 --> 00:44:09.340
Can you go on an ice run when we get there?
我们到了那里之后，你能去买点冰块吗？

915
00:44:10.460 --> 00:44:12.480
You do know I'm missing work for this.
你该知道我是请假来做这个的。

916
00:44:15.390 --> 00:44:17.110
It's day two of a paper airplane conteSt.
这可是纸飞机大赛的第二天。

917
00:44:17.230 --> 00:44:17.850
I think we're okay.
我想我们应该没问题。

918
00:44:18.750 --> 00:44:19.490
Fair point.
有道理。

919
00:44:21.070 --> 00:44:21.510
Amazing.
太棒了。

920
00:44:22.210 --> 00:44:25.450
And I want you to know Craig Robinson is so funny.
而且我想让你知道，克雷格·罗宾逊真的太搞笑了。

921
00:44:25.450 --> 00:44:29.470
From the minute he gets in that car to all of his reactions at the laboratory.
从他上车的那一刻起，到他在实验室里的所有反应，都很有趣。

922
00:44:30.030 --> 00:44:38.950
But what cracked me up, Jenna, watching it is when he says, hey, if they ask you about what we're like on set, tell them how we're always laughing all the time, you know?
但珍娜，看的时候最让我笑喷的是他说：嘿，如果他们问你我们在片场是什么样，就告诉他们我们总是笑个不停，你知道吧？

923
00:44:39.230 --> 00:44:48.450
And it was kind of funny because whenever we would do press junkets as a cast, one of the questions we got asked every single time was like, who's the prankster?
这挺有意思的，因为每当我们剧组参加媒体见面会时，被问到的每一个问题都是：谁是恶作剧大王？

924
00:44:48.590 --> 00:44:50.590
Who's making everyone laugh on set?
谁在片场把大家逗得哈哈大笑？

925
00:44:50.590 --> 00:44:51.470
It's true.
确实如此。

926
00:44:51.830 --> 00:44:56.510
I felt like this was like our writer's nod to like these same questions we would always get.
我觉得这是编剧在向我们总是被问到的这些问题致意。

927
00:44:56.970 --> 00:44:59.790
Well, I don't want to tell everybody in Hollywood what to do.
好吧，我不想教好莱坞的每个人该怎么做。

928
00:44:59.910 --> 00:45:06.530
But if you want Craig Robinson to be really funny in your project, put him in a car because I think he really shines in all the driving scenes.
但如果你想让克雷格·罗宾逊在你的项目中表现得非常搞笑，就把他放进车里，因为我觉得他在所有驾驶戏份中都非常出彩。

929
00:45:06.590 --> 00:45:14.170
Like when he's with Michael and Holly, when he and I had our driving scene, his show, Killing It, they spend a lot of time in a car.
就像他和迈克尔还有霍莉在一起时，还有我和他拍驾驶戏的时候，他的剧《杀手》里，他们花了很多时间在车里。

930
00:45:14.310 --> 00:45:14.870
They sure do.
他们确实是。

931
00:45:15.210 --> 00:45:16.750
And he is very funny in a car, everybody.
而且他在车里真的非常搞笑，各位。

932
00:45:17.070 --> 00:45:17.430
Yeah.
没错。

933
00:45:17.430 --> 00:45:18.910
I don't know what it is.
我也不知道为什么。

934
00:45:19.310 --> 00:45:25.190
Well, Daryl and Andy are going to arrive to this project and Carla is there.
好吧，达里尔和安迪要到达这个项目现场了，卡拉也在那儿。

935
00:45:25.430 --> 00:45:27.610
Carla seems a little interested in Daryl.
卡拉似乎对达里尔有点兴趣。

936
00:45:27.810 --> 00:45:32.370
She's like, hey, are you in this paper documentary as well?
她说：嘿，你也是来拍这个纸业纪录片的吗？

937
00:45:32.590 --> 00:45:33.630
Do you need an agent?
你需要经纪人吗？

938
00:45:34.130 --> 00:45:36.290
And Andy's like, no, no, no, no, no.
安迪说：不，不，不，不，不。

939
00:45:36.550 --> 00:45:37.430
He doesn't act.
他不演戏。

940
00:45:37.670 --> 00:45:40.090
And then Daryl has this throwaway line.
然后达里尔随口说了句台词。

941
00:45:40.190 --> 00:45:42.710
He says, well, I was in the Wiz in high school.
他说：好吧，我高中时演过《绿野仙踪》。

942
00:45:43.430 --> 00:45:44.970
That was not in the script.
那句台词剧本里没有。

943
00:45:45.250 --> 00:45:47.590
I don't know if they just found that on the day.
我不知道是不是他们当天临时想出来的。

944
00:45:49.630 --> 00:45:51.970
Well, I love this next scene.
好吧，我喜欢接下来的这一幕。

945
00:45:52.390 --> 00:45:57.690
Carla is going to show Andy that he's got a chair because all her actors get chairs.
卡拉要向安迪展示他有一把椅子，因为她所有的演员都有椅子。

946
00:45:58.010 --> 00:46:02.690
I thought this was very funny since not a single one of us ever had a chair on The Office.
我觉得这非常搞笑，因为我们《办公室》剧组里没一个人有过椅子。

947
00:46:02.910 --> 00:46:04.390
We did not have.
我们确实没有。

948
00:46:04.390 --> 00:46:05.210
Never got a chair.
从来没得到过椅子。

949
00:46:05.390 --> 00:46:06.190
A director's chair.
导演椅。

950
00:46:06.410 --> 00:46:06.610
No.
没有。

951
00:46:06.610 --> 00:46:08.110
But it is really funny.
但这真的很有趣。

952
00:46:08.270 --> 00:46:10.830
I loved it when she said, all my actors sit.
我特别喜欢她说的那句“我所有的演员都坐下”。

953
00:46:11.110 --> 00:46:12.210
Yes, exactly.
没错，就是这样。

954
00:46:12.630 --> 00:46:13.290
Very proudly.
非常自豪。

955
00:46:14.010 --> 00:46:18.070
I want you to know Halstead said that they did shoot in an actual laboratory.
我想让你们知道，Halstead说他们确实是在一个真正的实验室里拍摄的。

956
00:46:18.930 --> 00:46:20.310
This is an actual laboratory.
这就是一个真正的实验室。

957
00:46:20.610 --> 00:46:22.430
We got a fan question about it.
我们收到一个关于此的粉丝提问。

958
00:46:22.650 --> 00:46:23.370
Sarah M.
来自加拿大维多利亚的Sarah M.说：我是一名免疫学专业的博士生，我花了很多时间在实验室里。

959
00:46:23.550 --> 00:46:28.810
in Victoria, Canada said, I'm a PhD student specializing in immunology and I spend
我花了很多时间在实验室里。

960
00:46:28.810 --> 00:46:30.750
a significant amount of time in a lab.
我花了很多时间在实验室里。

961
00:46:31.010 --> 00:46:36.030
And when I see lab scenes in TV shows or movies, they tend to look far from realistic.
每当我在电视节目或电影里看到实验室场景时，它们看起来往往一点都不真实。

962
00:46:36.710 --> 00:46:38.950
Incredibly pristine and perfectly organized.
极其一尘不染，摆放得完美无缺。

963
00:46:39.390 --> 00:46:44.510
However, in this particular episode, I was genuinely impressed as it was evident to me
然而，在这一集中，我真的印象深刻，因为我很明显地看出，

964
00:46:44.510 --> 00:46:49.810
that the lab where Andy shot the laboratory safety video looked like a real working laboratory.
Andy拍摄实验室安全视频的那个实验室看起来像个真正的工作实验室。

965
00:46:50.370 --> 00:46:53.130
Well, Sarah, we did shoot in a real lab.
嗯，Sarah，我们确实是在一个真正的实验室里拍摄的。

966
00:46:53.510 --> 00:46:57.790
Steve Burgess said that there were no special safety issues at the lab, but there were some
Steve Burgess说实验室里没有什么特别的安全问题，但确实有些区域是禁止进入的。

967
00:46:57.790 --> 00:46:59.310
areas that were off limits.
区域是禁止进入的。

968
00:46:59.730 --> 00:47:04.510
It wasn't because anything like top secret was happening, but they just didn't want us
这不是因为有什么绝密的事情在发生，而是因为他们不想让我们弄乱他们的东西，毕竟那是真正的实验室。

969
00:47:04.510 --> 00:47:06.910
to mess their things up because they were a real lab.
毕竟那是真正的实验室。

970
00:47:07.310 --> 00:47:12.970
Steve said that we had our normal safety meetings, but we added one thing to the lab, which were
Steve说我们进行了常规的安全会议，但我们在实验室里增加了一样东西，那就是背景里的一些假冒泡烧杯。

971
00:47:12.970 --> 00:47:15.410
some fakie bubbling beakers in the background.
背景里的一些假冒泡烧杯。

972
00:47:16.550 --> 00:47:18.090
So, fakie beakers.
所以，假烧杯。

973
00:47:18.390 --> 00:47:20.170
Fakie beakers, real lab.
假烧杯，真实验室。

974
00:47:20.450 --> 00:47:21.170
That's right.
没错。

975
00:47:21.170 --> 00:47:25.450
Oh, I also want to give a guest star shout out to Kate Comer.
哦，我还想特别提一下客串明星Kate Comer。

976
00:47:25.670 --> 00:47:27.930
She's the woman who comes up to take Andy's photo.
她就是那个走过来给Andy拍照的女人。

977
00:47:28.990 --> 00:47:30.450
Yes, this is very funny.
是的，这非常有趣。

978
00:47:31.770 --> 00:47:34.110
Andy thinks, oh, it's starting the paparazzi.
Andy以为，哦，狗仔队要来了。

979
00:47:34.270 --> 00:47:37.570
And she's like, we just need a picture of your hair in case we burn it.
而她说的是，我们需要拍一张你头发的照片，以防我们把它烧坏了。

980
00:47:37.970 --> 00:47:38.230
Yes.
是的。

981
00:47:39.710 --> 00:47:44.050
This is something we had to do every day on the office several times a day.
这是我们在《办公室》剧组每天都要做几次的事情。

982
00:47:44.210 --> 00:47:45.590
They're called continuity photos.
它们被称为连贯性照片。

983
00:47:45.870 --> 00:47:46.850
Everyone takes them.
每个人都会拍。

984
00:47:47.050 --> 00:47:48.550
Hair and makeup take them.
发型和化妆组会拍。

985
00:47:48.690 --> 00:47:49.810
Wardrobe takes them.
服装组会拍。

986
00:47:50.250 --> 00:47:51.130
Props take them.
道具组会拍。

987
00:47:51.290 --> 00:47:52.870
And you have to pose.
而且你必须摆好姿势。

988
00:47:53.090 --> 00:47:56.630
And sometimes you have to give a profile, the back of your head, your hands.
有时你还得展示侧面、后脑勺和手。

989
00:47:57.050 --> 00:48:01.650
Oh, when Kim Ferry would do the complicated braids, she would have to take all these photos
哦，当Kim Ferry要做复杂的编发时，她得拍好多我后脑勺的照片。

990
00:48:01.650 --> 00:48:02.770
of the back of my head.
拍好多我后脑勺的照片。

991
00:48:03.610 --> 00:48:05.890
So that the braids matched every day.
这样每天的编发才能保持一致。

992
00:48:06.330 --> 00:48:10.910
And they would print these out and then they would put them in these elaborate binders.
他们会把这些照片打印出来，然后放进那些精细的活页夹里。

993
00:48:11.990 --> 00:48:16.190
And every once in a while, oh, talk about, you know how Toby's so excited to get out a
偶尔，哦，说到这个，你知道Toby对拿出活页夹有多兴奋吗？

994
00:48:16.190 --> 00:48:16.550
binder?
活页夹？

995
00:48:17.230 --> 00:48:22.690
Talk about how excited hair and makeup was when we would have to go back to a previous episode
说说当我们需要回到之前的剧集重拍某些片段或补拍镜头时，发型和化妆组有多兴奋吧。

996
00:48:22.690 --> 00:48:26.270
and reshoot something or create extra footage.
补拍镜头。

997
00:48:26.430 --> 00:48:29.050
They had the binder with the hair and the makeup.
他们有记录发型和妆容的活页夹。

998
00:48:29.090 --> 00:48:29.140
Yes.
是的。

999
00:48:29.490 --> 00:48:30.350
She would go in.
她会走进去。

1000
00:48:30.430 --> 00:48:31.770
She'd be like, I got it.
她会说，我找到了。

1001
00:48:31.770 --> 00:48:37.090
You want to recreate season five, episode 13, scene 4A?
你想重现第五季第13集第4A场吗？

1002
00:48:37.350 --> 00:48:40.610
And she'd flip to the page and there all of our hair would be.
她会翻到那一页，上面就有我们所有人的发型。

1003
00:48:40.770 --> 00:48:44.030
And she would be like, Angela, you were half up, half down.
她会说，安吉拉，你当时是一半扎起，一半披着。

1004
00:48:44.430 --> 00:48:46.110
Jenna, you were in a ponytail.
珍娜，你当时扎的是马尾。

1005
00:48:47.170 --> 00:48:52.930
Lady, part of my digital clutter and photos from this episode, I took a lot of our crew.
女士，作为我数字杂物和这一集照片的一部分，我拍了很多我们剧组人员的照片。

1006
00:48:53.390 --> 00:48:54.290
You did?
你拍了？

1007
00:48:54.290 --> 00:48:54.750
Yeah.
对。

1008
00:48:54.950 --> 00:48:58.790
So I have hair and makeup backstage, you know, at their tables.
所以我拍了后台化妆间里，你知道，在他们桌子旁边的发型师和化妆师。

1009
00:48:58.930 --> 00:49:03.730
And I have our crew all in the warehouse as we were figuring out the paper airplane scenes.
还有我们在仓库里琢磨纸飞机场景时，拍了我们所有的剧组人员。

1010
00:49:03.950 --> 00:49:05.630
I'll put all of them in stories.
我会把它们都发到快拍里。

1011
00:49:05.810 --> 00:49:08.390
It just, I just love seeing everyone.
我就是，我就是喜欢看到大家。

1012
00:49:08.990 --> 00:49:12.990
Well, speaking of the warehouse, the competition is underway.
说到仓库，比赛正在进行中。

1013
00:49:12.990 --> 00:49:15.610
And it's going to start with Kevin versus Angela.
首先是凯文对阵安吉拉。

1014
00:49:16.190 --> 00:49:20.790
Yeah, Kevin has a pretty fancy looking plane and Dwight questions it.
没错，凯文的飞机看起来很花哨，德怀特对此提出了质疑。

1015
00:49:20.910 --> 00:49:21.990
He's looking out for Angela.
他在替安吉拉把关。

1016
00:49:22.230 --> 00:49:24.350
He's like, you made that paper airplane?
他说，这纸飞机是你做的？

1017
00:49:24.670 --> 00:49:28.270
And Brian's performance is so great right here.
布莱恩在这里的表演真是太棒了。

1018
00:49:28.450 --> 00:49:31.250
Like he literally, it's like he manifests a sweat.
他简直，就像是凭空冒出了一身汗。

1019
00:49:31.890 --> 00:49:34.670
Kevin's like, well, sort of.
凯文说，嗯，算是吧。

1020
00:49:34.830 --> 00:49:37.390
And then we find out that Kevin bought it online.
然后我们发现凯文是在网上买的。

1021
00:49:38.030 --> 00:49:38.390
Yeah.
没错。

1022
00:49:38.910 --> 00:49:41.750
So they call for a refold.
所以他们要求重折。

1023
00:49:42.150 --> 00:49:43.750
He has to refold.
他必须重折。

1024
00:49:43.870 --> 00:49:46.050
And you're going to see him at like a table.
你会看到他在桌子旁。

1025
00:49:46.350 --> 00:49:52.390
And he's been folding planes forever, trying to make a plane.
他折了半天飞机，试图折出一架来。

1026
00:49:52.990 --> 00:49:53.970
Guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1027
00:49:55.070 --> 00:49:56.790
Facts coming your way.
冷知识来了。

1028
00:49:57.250 --> 00:49:58.330
Paper airplane facts.
关于纸飞机的冷知识。

1029
00:49:58.330 --> 00:49:59.970
Facts inspired by this moment.
受这一刻启发的冷知识。

1030
00:50:00.350 --> 00:50:04.910
Do you know what the most paper airplanes made in one hour is?
你知道一小时内折纸飞机数量的世界纪录是多少吗？

1031
00:50:05.250 --> 00:50:06.630
In one hour?
一小时内？

1032
00:50:07.390 --> 00:50:15.110
Someone made 12,026 paper airplanes, which is about one every 3.3 seconds.
有人折了12026架纸飞机，大约每3.3秒一架。

1033
00:50:15.410 --> 00:50:22.550
Do you think the person that did that has like little special like bandages on their fingers?
你觉得那个人手指上是不是贴了什么特殊的创可贴之类的？

1034
00:50:22.550 --> 00:50:27.050
Like how my mom has that little rubber thing you put on your finger when you're sewing?
就像我妈缝纫时戴在手指上的那种橡胶指套？

1035
00:50:27.390 --> 00:50:28.110
You muSt.
肯定得戴。

1036
00:50:28.330 --> 00:50:33.310
Because the paper cuts, I feel like, are all over the place.
因为我觉得纸割伤肯定到处都是。

1037
00:50:33.610 --> 00:50:33.810
Yeah.
没错。

1038
00:50:34.670 --> 00:50:40.890
Also, I mean, what is the quality of a paper airplane that you made in 3.3 seconds?
而且，我是说，3.3秒折出来的纸飞机质量能好到哪去？

1039
00:50:41.190 --> 00:50:41.590
I don't know.
我不知道。

1040
00:50:41.750 --> 00:50:43.130
There's no quality control here.
这里根本没有质量控制。

1041
00:50:43.290 --> 00:50:43.370
There's no quality.
根本没质量可言。

1042
00:50:43.370 --> 00:50:44.390
It's just volume.
纯粹是拼数量。

1043
00:50:45.070 --> 00:50:45.370
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1044
00:50:45.490 --> 00:50:51.850
I also found out that the fastest time to fold and then throw a paper airplane.
我还查到了折好并投掷纸飞机的最快时间。

1045
00:50:51.850 --> 00:50:56.730
So in this case, you actually had to make like a flyable device.
所以在这个案例里，你实际上得做出一个能飞的装置。

1046
00:50:56.730 --> 00:51:03.350
So fold and throw, the fastest time is 7.03 seconds.
所以折叠加投掷，最快时间是7.03秒。

1047
00:51:04.130 --> 00:51:06.170
Seven seconds?
七秒？

1048
00:51:06.610 --> 00:51:07.130
Yeah.
对。

1049
00:51:07.350 --> 00:51:08.590
7.03.
7.03秒。

1050
00:51:09.010 --> 00:51:11.310
You would fold and then throw it and it flew.
你得折好然后扔出去，而且它还得飞起来。

1051
00:51:11.830 --> 00:51:14.210
That is the fastest time.
那是目前最快的纪录。

1052
00:51:14.610 --> 00:51:15.410
That's crazy.
太疯狂了。

1053
00:51:15.410 --> 00:51:27.850
And so that's why I'm like, okay, if the most paper airplanes made in one hour was like a little over 12,000, they're having to fold like these paper airplanes in 3.3 seconds.
所以我当时就在想，好吧，如果一小时内折出的纸飞机最多也就一万两千多架，那他们平均每3.3秒就得折出一架。

1054
00:51:27.850 --> 00:51:32.470
But in order to fold and throw one that flies, the fastest is 7 seconds.
但要折出一架能飞的纸飞机，最快也要7秒。

1055
00:51:32.470 --> 00:51:37.030
I'm thinking a lot of those 12,000 airplanes were not flight worthy.
我觉得那一万两千架飞机里，很多根本飞不起来。

1056
00:51:37.550 --> 00:51:38.530
You know what I'm saying?
你明白我的意思吗？

1057
00:51:38.970 --> 00:51:39.470
You think?
你觉得呢？

1058
00:51:41.150 --> 00:51:50.170
Similar to Kevin's pile, which looks like a bunch of just randomly folded paper and maybe 20% look like airplanes.
就像凯文那堆纸一样，看起来就是一堆乱折的纸，可能只有20%看起来像飞机。

1059
00:51:50.430 --> 00:51:51.070
I don't know.
我不知道。

1060
00:51:51.070 --> 00:51:51.530
Yeah.
是啊。

1061
00:51:51.830 --> 00:51:52.510
He's struggling.
他正费劲呢。

1062
00:51:53.050 --> 00:51:58.990
I asked Warren and Halstead if there were any deleted scenes that they wish could have made it in this episode.
我问过沃伦和霍尔斯特德，有没有什么被删减的片段是他们希望能在这一集里保留的。

1063
00:51:59.150 --> 00:52:01.430
And Halstead shared a talking head that they wrote.
霍尔斯特德分享了一个他们写过的采访片段。

1064
00:52:01.610 --> 00:52:02.790
It's in the shooting draft.
就在拍摄剧本里。

1065
00:52:03.410 --> 00:52:04.850
And it is really funny.
而且真的很有趣。

1066
00:52:05.010 --> 00:52:05.630
I'm going to read it.
我要读一下。

1067
00:52:05.970 --> 00:52:07.450
It's Dwight.
是德怀特说的。

1068
00:52:07.630 --> 00:52:12.050
And he's just called Kevin out that Kevin did not make that paper airplane.
他直接拆穿了凯文，说那架纸飞机根本不是凯文折的。

1069
00:52:12.750 --> 00:52:14.610
And here was a talking head.
这是当时的采访片段。

1070
00:52:14.990 --> 00:52:15.890
Dwight says,
德怀特说，

1071
00:52:16.030 --> 00:52:18.310
There is no way he built that plane.
他绝对不可能折出那架飞机。

1072
00:52:18.830 --> 00:52:23.790
I once watched him spend 20 minutes trying to put an envelope into a letter.
我曾亲眼看着他花了20分钟，试图把信封塞进信里。

1073
00:52:24.070 --> 00:52:24.910
You heard me.
你没听错。

1074
00:52:25.470 --> 00:52:26.670
You heard me.
你没听错。

1075
00:52:28.190 --> 00:52:29.850
Anyway, that cracked me up, too.
总之，那段也把我逗乐了。

1076
00:52:30.110 --> 00:52:30.330
That's pretty great.
那真的很棒。

1077
00:52:30.730 --> 00:52:35.310
Well, something we should mention is that Angela has taken notice of Dwight's behavior here.
对了，我们应该提一下，安吉拉注意到了德怀特在这里的表现。

1078
00:52:35.670 --> 00:52:36.170
Yeah.
没错。

1079
00:52:36.210 --> 00:52:37.250
She has a talking head.
她有一个采访片段。

1080
00:52:37.530 --> 00:52:38.250
She does.
确实有。

1081
00:52:38.250 --> 00:52:39.330
She says to camera,
她对着镜头说，

1082
00:52:39.570 --> 00:52:40.870
Was Dwight rooting for me?
德怀特是在支持我吗？

1083
00:52:41.010 --> 00:52:41.250
Hmm.
嗯。

1084
00:52:41.410 --> 00:52:42.410
I hadn't noticed.
我之前都没注意到。

1085
00:52:42.930 --> 00:52:43.310
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1086
00:52:43.770 --> 00:52:44.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1087
00:52:44.590 --> 00:52:47.010
She's very delighted by this.
她对此感到非常高兴。

1088
00:52:47.010 --> 00:52:48.330
She sure is.
她确实很高兴。

1089
00:52:48.550 --> 00:52:54.770
Back in the bullpen, Jim has brought Pam a cup of tea, which she appreciates.
回到办公区，吉姆给帕姆带了一杯茶，帕姆很感激。

1090
00:52:55.030 --> 00:52:55.790
She does.
她是挺感激的。

1091
00:52:56.430 --> 00:53:03.950
He shares that the truth is he was going in the kitchen anyway because he felt like a cup of tea for himself.
吉姆说实话，他本来就要去厨房，因为他自己也想喝杯茶。

1092
00:53:04.410 --> 00:53:10.110
And then Pam shares her truth, which is she actually switched to coffee back in March.
然后帕姆也说了实话，其实她早在三月份就改喝咖啡了。

1093
00:53:10.110 --> 00:53:13.510
But she still appreciates the gesture.
但她还是很感激他的心意。

1094
00:53:14.390 --> 00:53:14.550
Yeah.
是啊。

1095
00:53:15.130 --> 00:53:18.370
So there was a talking head here that they cut.
所以这里原本有一个被剪掉的采访片段。

1096
00:53:18.910 --> 00:53:19.250
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1097
00:53:19.970 --> 00:53:22.790
Jim was going to say something like,
吉姆原本打算说类似这样的话：

1098
00:53:23.810 --> 00:53:25.590
Wow, she switched to coffee.
哇，她改喝咖啡了。

1099
00:53:26.130 --> 00:53:28.830
And then he was going to pause and say something like,
然后他会停顿一下，再说类似这样的话：

1100
00:53:29.750 --> 00:53:32.250
But she still likes mixed berries, right?
但她还是喜欢混合浆果口味的，对吧？

1101
00:53:32.490 --> 00:53:35.250
Like he was going to reference the mixed berries yogurt.
就好像他会提到那个混合浆果酸奶一样。

1102
00:53:35.250 --> 00:53:36.210
I know.
我知道。

1103
00:53:36.690 --> 00:53:37.030
Hmm.
嗯。

1104
00:53:37.850 --> 00:53:41.170
You know, when I saw this scene, it really hit me.
你知道吗，当我看到这一幕时，我真的很有感触。

1105
00:53:41.290 --> 00:53:43.570
I was like, this is significant.
我当时就想，这意义重大。

1106
00:53:43.730 --> 00:53:46.290
You don't know her morning drink.
你竟然不知道她早上喝什么。

1107
00:53:46.410 --> 00:53:55.370
Like you are so disconnected from one another that you don't know this big piece of information that's a part of her every day.
就好像你们彼此之间如此疏离，连她每天生活中这么重要的一部分信息都不知道。

1108
00:53:55.570 --> 00:53:56.530
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

1109
00:53:56.690 --> 00:53:58.410
This is the everyday intimacy.
这就是日常的亲密感。

1110
00:53:58.810 --> 00:54:01.730
And it is missing from Jim and Pam's life.
而这在吉姆和帕姆的生活中缺失了。

1111
00:54:01.730 --> 00:54:07.170
And I would say I think it's the very small little things in life.
我想说，我认为正是生活中那些微不足道的小事。

1112
00:54:07.650 --> 00:54:09.890
That's how you know someone truly.
那才是你真正了解一个人的方式。

1113
00:54:10.270 --> 00:54:13.070
It's very easy to know the big things.
了解大事很容易。

1114
00:54:13.250 --> 00:54:13.610
Yes.
是的。

1115
00:54:13.710 --> 00:54:18.590
You know, but it's the very small intimate things that separate a relationship.
你知道，但正是那些细微而亲密的事情才让一段关系与众不同。

1116
00:54:19.250 --> 00:54:19.550
Yes.
是的。

1117
00:54:20.530 --> 00:54:21.170
Exactly.
没错。

1118
00:54:21.570 --> 00:54:23.490
Well, that's just good writing, right?
嗯，这就是优秀的剧本，对吧？

1119
00:54:23.830 --> 00:54:24.210
I know.
我知道。

1120
00:54:24.390 --> 00:54:25.050
It's just really good writing.
这剧本写得真好。

1121
00:54:25.350 --> 00:54:26.410
Really, really good writing.
真的，写得太好了。

1122
00:54:27.030 --> 00:54:35.370
Well, speaking of really good writing that didn't make it in, back at the laboratory, there was a scene that would have gone here.
说到那些没能放进正片的优秀剧本，在实验室里，本来还有一场戏。

1123
00:54:36.170 --> 00:54:41.250
And Andy, because it's an industrial shoot, had to do his own hair and makeup, Jenna.
安迪因为是在工业拍摄现场，不得不自己化妆做造型，珍娜。

1124
00:54:41.750 --> 00:54:42.130
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1125
00:54:42.670 --> 00:54:44.990
What does Andy know about hair and makeup?
安迪懂什么化妆造型啊？

1126
00:54:45.190 --> 00:54:47.070
He knows the world of the theater.
他可是混过戏剧圈的。

1127
00:54:47.550 --> 00:54:48.290
Oh, boy.
天哪。

1128
00:54:48.490 --> 00:54:50.690
He does full stage makeup.
他会化全套舞台妆。

1129
00:54:50.690 --> 00:55:00.210
He, penciled in his eyebrows, he has on white eyeshadow, he has on that orange kind of base, you know, like that heavy foundation.
他用铅笔画了眉毛，涂了白色眼影，还抹了那种橙色的底妆，你知道的，就是那种厚重的粉底。

1130
00:55:00.530 --> 00:55:00.730
Yeah.
是啊。

1131
00:55:00.970 --> 00:55:04.410
With bright red, like blushed cheeks.
还有鲜红的腮红。

1132
00:55:05.010 --> 00:55:07.530
Well, they need to see you from the back row.
毕竟得让最后一排的观众看清你。

1133
00:55:07.970 --> 00:55:08.770
From the balcony.
从楼座看过去。

1134
00:55:09.370 --> 00:55:12.470
And you have those harsh lights on you on the theater, you know?
而且剧院的灯光又那么刺眼，你懂的吧？

1135
00:55:13.410 --> 00:55:14.810
Oh, my gosh.
我的天呐。

1136
00:55:14.950 --> 00:55:19.330
He walks into the laboratory in his lab coat with this stage makeup.
他穿着实验服，顶着那副舞台妆走进了实验室。

1137
00:55:19.950 --> 00:55:22.010
Everyone's reactions are hilarious.
大家的反应太搞笑了。

1138
00:55:22.590 --> 00:55:24.570
And I wanted you to hear the clip.
我想让你听听这段录音。

1139
00:55:24.770 --> 00:55:25.870
It's in deleted scenes.
在删减片段里。

1140
00:55:26.070 --> 00:55:26.790
I cannot wait.
我等不及了。

1141
00:55:27.310 --> 00:55:27.770
Ta-da!
当当！

1142
00:55:28.570 --> 00:55:30.190
Meet the lab assistant.
见见实验室助理。

1143
00:55:30.890 --> 00:55:32.430
Ooh, what's with the clown face?
噢，你这小丑脸是怎么回事？

1144
00:55:32.630 --> 00:55:33.950
It's professional stage makeup.
这是专业的舞台妆。

1145
00:55:34.070 --> 00:55:35.910
Keeps from washing out under the harsh lights.
防止在强光下显得脸色苍白。

1146
00:55:36.170 --> 00:55:38.110
I learned it when I was Nakey Poo in the Mikado.
我演《天皇》里的“裸体小宝”时学的。

1147
00:55:39.070 --> 00:55:39.890
Andrew Bernard?
安德鲁·伯纳德？

1148
00:55:40.290 --> 00:55:40.470
Yeah.
到。

1149
00:55:41.390 --> 00:55:42.530
What's on your face?
你脸上涂的什么？

1150
00:55:42.790 --> 00:55:44.610
A little of the old grease paint, governor.
一点老派油彩，长官。

1151
00:55:45.710 --> 00:55:47.150
Lashes sold separately.
睫毛膏需另购。

1152
00:55:47.630 --> 00:55:51.090
Um, I'm going to need him to take this off immediately, okay?
嗯，我需要他立刻把它摘掉，好吗？

1153
00:55:51.270 --> 00:55:51.370
Okay.
好的。

1154
00:55:51.490 --> 00:55:53.330
Question, is it too dark?
请问，这颜色太深了吗？

1155
00:55:53.350 --> 00:55:54.930
Because this is Trinidad.
因为这是特立尼达色。

1156
00:55:55.170 --> 00:55:59.310
I also have Brazilian Matador or Man of Athens.
我还有巴西斗牛士色或者雅典男人色。

1157
00:55:59.630 --> 00:56:00.790
How about no makeup at all?
如果不化妆怎么样？

1158
00:56:00.890 --> 00:56:01.290
No makeup.
不化妆。

1159
00:56:01.610 --> 00:56:02.190
No makeup.
不化妆。

1160
00:56:02.270 --> 00:56:02.590
Great.
太好了。

1161
00:56:02.750 --> 00:56:03.290
I can do that.
我可以做到。

1162
00:56:03.450 --> 00:56:04.210
But, question.
但是，有个问题。

1163
00:56:04.450 --> 00:56:08.010
New to the area, is there a makeup remover store nearby?
我刚搬到这附近，请问这附近有卖卸妆产品的店吗？

1164
00:56:08.430 --> 00:56:09.750
Uh, you'll just use soap.
呃，你直接用肥皂洗就行。

1165
00:56:10.550 --> 00:56:11.050
Wow.
哇。

1166
00:56:11.310 --> 00:56:11.810
Yeah.
是啊。

1167
00:56:12.070 --> 00:56:12.930
I love it.
我喜欢。

1168
00:56:13.690 --> 00:56:18.030
Halstead said, when Ed said Man of Athens, it made everyone crack up.
霍尔斯特德说，当埃德提到“雅典男人”这个色号时，大家都笑喷了。

1169
00:56:18.710 --> 00:56:20.990
Well, I have a guest star shout out.
对了，我有个客串明星要提一下。

1170
00:56:21.290 --> 00:56:23.250
Ooh, I bet I know who it is.
噢，我敢打赌我知道是谁。

1171
00:56:23.730 --> 00:56:25.190
Yes, I know you do.
没错，我知道你知道。

1172
00:56:25.410 --> 00:56:27.110
It's the producer on set.
就是片场的那位制片人。

1173
00:56:27.350 --> 00:56:31.650
He was played by an old improv friend of mine and Warren's, Pete Holney.
他是由我和沃伦的一位即兴表演老友，皮特·霍尔尼饰演的。

1174
00:56:32.050 --> 00:56:35.270
Pete has been in so many movies and television shows.
皮特出演过很多电影和电视剧。

1175
00:56:35.270 --> 00:56:38.070
You can catch him in Criminal Minds right now.
你现在可以在《犯罪心理》里看到他。

1176
00:56:38.250 --> 00:56:43.070
He was in Jury Duty by our very own Lee Eisenberg and Gene Stepnitzky.
他还出演了由我们自己的李·艾森伯格和吉恩·斯图尼茨基制作的《陪审义务》。

1177
00:56:43.750 --> 00:56:46.530
He's in Monsters Season 2 on Netflix.
他还在Netflix的《怪物》第二季里有演出。

1178
00:56:46.750 --> 00:56:52.970
If you're a fan of the movie Elf, Pete and his real twin brother, Patrick Holney, are the
如果你是电影《精灵》的粉丝，皮特和他现实中的双胞胎兄弟帕特里克·霍尔尼，就是片中那对

1179
00:56:52.970 --> 00:56:54.190
twin elves in the movie.
双胞胎精灵。

1180
00:56:54.770 --> 00:57:01.890
And Warren shared with me that it was really a really fun shoot day for him because Pete was there and they'd known each other for so long.
沃伦跟我分享说，那天拍摄对他来说非常开心，因为皮特在场，而且他们认识很久了。

1181
00:57:02.090 --> 00:57:05.330
And that he was always pitching Pete for roles in the office.
他说他一直都在向《办公室》剧组力荐皮特。

1182
00:57:05.330 --> 00:57:08.090
And so he was so glad it finally worked out.
所以他很高兴这次终于成行了。

1183
00:57:08.090 --> 00:57:15.750
And I reached out to Pete and, lady, he has a really sweet story about Alison Jones, and I thought you should hear it.
我联系了皮特，女士，他关于艾莉森·琼斯有一个非常暖心的故事，我觉得你应该听听。

1184
00:57:15.970 --> 00:57:16.450
Okay.
好的。

1185
00:57:16.950 --> 00:57:23.630
An interesting thing is, like, casting directors remember actors if they're good.
有趣的是，选角导演如果觉得演员不错，是会记住他们的。

1186
00:57:24.650 --> 00:57:33.530
And when you audition for things and you don't get the part, the amazing thing is, is that the casting director's mind has to remember actors.
当你去试镜却没选上时，神奇的地方在于，选角导演的大脑必须得记住这些演员。

1187
00:57:33.530 --> 00:57:35.610
And when things come up, they remember them.
当有合适的角色出现时，他们就会想起这些人。

1188
00:57:35.610 --> 00:57:46.430
So Alison Jones, who is the casting director of the show, remembered me from, I don't know, auditioning the first time.
所以，该剧的选角导演艾莉森·琼斯，从我第一次试镜时就记住我了，我也不知道为什么。

1189
00:57:46.570 --> 00:57:52.190
But the weird thing was, is that she did something wonderful to me once.
但奇怪的是，她曾经对我做过一件很棒的事。

1190
00:57:52.190 --> 00:57:58.450
I was at The Grove, which is like a big shopping mall here in Los Angeles in Farmer's Market.
当时我在格罗夫购物中心，就是洛杉矶农夫市场那边的一个大型购物中心。

1191
00:57:58.690 --> 00:58:03.550
And I was going up an escalator and I just heard this voice yelling,
我正坐自动扶梯上去，突然听到一个声音在大喊：

1192
00:58:03.550 --> 00:58:07.750
Peter, Peter, Peter Holney.
“皮特，皮特，皮特·霍尔尼。”

1193
00:58:08.270 --> 00:58:11.970
And I was like, who the hell is screaming my name?
我当时心想，到底是谁在喊我的名字？

1194
00:58:12.270 --> 00:58:15.950
And all these people are like looking around, seeing who the hell this Peter Holney is.
周围的人都在四处张望，看这个皮特·霍尔尼到底是何方神圣。

1195
00:58:16.270 --> 00:58:22.830
And I looked down and as the escalator's going up, I'm going down.
我往下看，扶梯正在上升，而她在往下走。

1196
00:58:22.830 --> 00:58:26.070
And I see this woman waving frantically.
我看到一个女人在疯狂地挥手。

1197
00:58:26.450 --> 00:58:29.350
And I looked at her like, who are you?
我看着她，心想：你是谁？

1198
00:58:29.630 --> 00:58:31.790
I can't even put my brain couldn't process it.
我的大脑甚至无法处理这个信息。

1199
00:58:32.050 --> 00:58:37.490
And she goes, it's me, Alison Jones from casting.
然后她说：“是我，选角导演艾莉森·琼斯。”

1200
00:58:37.490 --> 00:58:41.430
And then all of a sudden, as she was going up, I was going down.
就在那一瞬间，她向上走，我向下走，我们就这样错开了。

1201
00:58:41.690 --> 00:58:43.030
She just kind of disappeared.
她就那么消失了。

1202
00:58:43.870 --> 00:58:45.470
And I was just dumbstruck.
我当时完全惊呆了。

1203
00:58:45.670 --> 00:58:50.190
I didn't know what to do because I've never been cast by her yet.
我不知道该怎么办，因为她之前还没选过我。

1204
00:58:50.190 --> 00:58:53.530
And I was just amazed that she remembered me.
我很惊讶她竟然还记得我。

1205
00:58:54.510 --> 00:59:02.130
And I was like, oh, my God, Alison Jones knows my name, knows my face and and said my last name correctly.
我当时心想，天哪，艾莉森·琼斯竟然知道我的名字，认得我的脸，而且还准确地念出了我的姓氏。

1206
00:59:02.690 --> 00:59:10.910
And I just thought that was just a wonderful, I mean, all day long, I was walking around with my head up high going, all right.
我觉得这真是太棒了，那一整天我都是昂首挺胸地走来走去，心想，好吧。

1207
00:59:11.090 --> 00:59:11.790
All right, Hollywood.
好吧，好莱坞。

1208
00:59:12.250 --> 00:59:14.230
You guys think I'm something special.
你们觉得我还是有点料的。

1209
00:59:16.860 --> 00:59:18.300
I love Alison.
我爱艾莉森。

1210
00:59:18.820 --> 00:59:19.420
I do, too.
我也是。

1211
00:59:19.600 --> 00:59:21.640
Can't you just see her yelling, hey?
你能想象她大喊“嘿”的样子吗？

1212
00:59:21.860 --> 00:59:25.440
I mean, she is just a just a wonderful person.
我是说，她真的是个非常棒的人。

1213
00:59:25.520 --> 00:59:29.640
And I just love that story and wanted to share that side of her with everyone that we know.
我很喜欢这个故事，也想和大家分享她那一面。

1214
00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:31.260
Yes, I love that.
是的，我喜欢这个故事。

1215
00:59:31.260 --> 00:59:35.400
And here's Pete's story about how this role came to be for him.
接下来是皮特关于他如何得到这个角色的故事。

1216
00:59:35.920 --> 00:59:41.820
I was flying home to Chicago for Christmas with my kids and my lovely wife.
当时我正带着孩子们和我可爱的妻子飞回芝加哥过圣诞节。

1217
00:59:42.000 --> 00:59:43.120
And we just landed.
我们刚落地。

1218
00:59:43.800 --> 00:59:47.080
And out of nowhere, I got a call from my agent.
突然间，我接到了经纪人的电话。

1219
00:59:47.140 --> 00:59:49.960
And they said, hey, you just booked the office.
他们说，嘿，你刚拿下了《办公室》的角色。

1220
00:59:50.240 --> 00:59:51.920
And I kind of laughed.
我当时笑了笑。

1221
00:59:52.000 --> 00:59:53.080
I go, ha, I'm in Chicago.
我说，哈，我在芝加哥呢。

1222
00:59:53.080 --> 00:59:53.680
You know that.
你知道的。

1223
00:59:53.820 --> 00:59:54.340
I booked out.
我申请了休假。

1224
00:59:54.580 --> 00:59:57.900
Alison Jones just called up and said, she wants to book you.
艾莉森·琼斯刚打电话来说，她想让你出演。

1225
00:59:58.040 --> 00:59:58.940
Well, I'm in Chicago.
可是我在芝加哥啊。

1226
00:59:58.940 --> 01:00:06.200
We just landed and I'm building a snowman with my daughter, Sophia, because they've never seen snow before because they live in L.A.
我们刚落地，我正和女儿索菲亚堆雪人呢，因为她们住在洛杉矶，从没见过雪。

1227
01:00:06.660 --> 01:00:12.580
Anyways, so they were like, you need to either do this or just decline it.
总之，他们当时说，你要么接受，要么拒绝。

1228
01:00:12.580 --> 01:00:21.680
So I thought for a minute as I put like the carrot into the snowman's face, well, I'm not going to let this opportunity pass me by.
我一边把胡萝卜插到雪人的脸上，一边想了一会儿，好吧，我不能错过这个机会。

1229
01:00:23.600 --> 01:00:30.640
I guess my Christmas vacation is going to be put on hold because I'm flying back to be on the office.
看来我的圣诞假期要暂停了，因为我要飞回去拍《办公室》了。

1230
01:00:31.260 --> 01:00:35.980
That day, I think I booked a flight and got there the next morning.
那天我好像就订了机票，第二天早上就到了。

1231
01:00:37.220 --> 01:00:40.940
And it was just amazing because those kind of things never happen.
这真是太神奇了，因为这种事通常不会发生。

1232
01:00:41.180 --> 01:00:44.340
You don't just usually book a job without even auditioning for it.
你通常不会在没试镜的情况下就直接拿到工作。

1233
01:00:45.160 --> 01:00:48.260
But Alison Jones just remembered me and gave me the part.
但艾莉森·琼斯记住了我，并把这个角色给了我。

1234
01:00:49.620 --> 01:00:53.140
Well, that is really special when you're just like, hey, you got the role.
当你听到“嘿，你拿到角色了”的时候，那感觉真的很特别。

1235
01:00:53.300 --> 01:00:53.960
You're like, what?
你会想，什么？

1236
01:00:54.440 --> 01:00:56.980
Yeah, you're like a role I didn't even know was happening.
是啊，就像是一个你甚至不知道存在的角色。

1237
01:00:56.980 --> 01:00:58.320
It existed, yeah.
它确实存在，没错。

1238
01:00:58.580 --> 01:01:07.700
And Warren told me he was really happy because when you have an episode that is your episode that you wrote, you are in direct communication with the director.
沃伦告诉我他非常高兴，因为当你负责编剧那一集时，你可以直接与导演沟通。

1239
01:01:08.080 --> 01:01:11.860
And that doesn't normally happen when it's not your episode.
如果不是你负责的那一集，通常不会这样。

1240
01:01:11.860 --> 01:01:13.860
You don't really go to the director, right?
你通常不会去找导演，对吧？

1241
01:01:13.980 --> 01:01:14.920
You don't pitch anything.
你不会去提任何建议。

1242
01:01:15.100 --> 01:01:24.340
But because it was his episode, he was able to talk directly to Jesse and say, we've got this great guy and really push that through for Pete.
但因为那是他负责的一集，他可以直接和杰西谈，说我们有个很棒的人选，并极力为皮特争取。

1243
01:01:24.960 --> 01:01:30.380
Well, I'll tell you what, as an actor, if you want to get a job, just leave town.
我跟你说，作为演员，如果你想找工作，就离开城里。

1244
01:01:30.680 --> 01:01:31.700
Well, that's true.
没错，确实如此。

1245
01:01:32.020 --> 01:01:32.420
Anytime.
随时都行。

1246
01:01:33.300 --> 01:01:33.440
Yes.
是的。

1247
01:01:34.060 --> 01:01:38.820
As soon as your friend tells you they're getting married out of town, you're going to book a job.
只要你的朋友告诉你他们要出城结婚，你准能接到工作。

1248
01:01:39.280 --> 01:01:41.220
It happened with me and you, Angela.
我和你就发生过这种情况，安吉拉。

1249
01:01:41.680 --> 01:01:41.900
Yeah.
是啊。

1250
01:01:42.120 --> 01:01:46.600
When you and Josh set your wedding date, I was like, I'm so excited.
当你和乔什定下婚礼日期时，我当时心想，我太兴奋了。

1251
01:01:46.600 --> 01:01:50.080
I'm going to be there the whole week with you as you get ready.
我会整整一周都陪着你，帮你一起做准备。

1252
01:01:51.500 --> 01:01:53.520
Booked a movie with Ben Stiller.
接了一部本·斯蒂勒的电影。

1253
01:01:53.680 --> 01:01:54.020
Yep.
没错。

1254
01:01:54.020 --> 01:01:56.980
Was in Montreal, flew in the morning of your wedding.
当时在蒙特利尔，婚礼当天早上才飞回来。

1255
01:01:57.800 --> 01:02:00.580
I did tell them I have to be at this wedding.
我确实跟他们说了我必须参加这场婚礼。

1256
01:02:01.060 --> 01:02:02.520
I was so thankful.
我当时特别感激。

1257
01:02:02.560 --> 01:02:05.220
And I was like, oh, my God, you're going to be so tired.
我当时就想，天哪，你肯定会累坏的。

1258
01:02:05.740 --> 01:02:07.140
But you got there.
但你还是赶到了。

1259
01:02:08.000 --> 01:02:09.060
But it's true.
但这是真的。

1260
01:02:09.180 --> 01:02:09.600
It's true.
确实如此。

1261
01:02:09.780 --> 01:02:14.240
I mean, you and I had some plans this next week and I booked a job.
我是说，你我下周本来有些计划，结果我接了个工作。

1262
01:02:14.460 --> 01:02:15.400
You booked a job.
你接了个工作。

1263
01:02:15.400 --> 01:02:16.320
And here we are.
然后我们就这样了。

1264
01:02:16.460 --> 01:02:19.400
Here we are on a Saturday morning with Cassie.
周六早上和凯西在一起。

1265
01:02:19.620 --> 01:02:20.100
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1266
01:02:20.220 --> 01:02:20.800
Thank you, ladies.
谢谢你们，女士们。

1267
01:02:21.040 --> 01:02:21.100
It's how it goes.
事情就是这样。

1268
01:02:21.280 --> 01:02:22.780
Leave town and you'll book a job.
一离开城里，你就会接到工作。

1269
01:02:22.960 --> 01:02:23.160
Yep.
没错。

1270
01:02:23.160 --> 01:02:24.100
Well, let's see.
好吧，让我们看看。

1271
01:02:24.220 --> 01:02:29.240
They're going to start rolling on Andy and he's making a number of strange choices.
他们要开始拍安迪了，他做了一系列奇怪的选择。

1272
01:02:29.960 --> 01:02:30.680
Yes.
是的。

1273
01:02:31.080 --> 01:02:31.520
Yes.
没错。

1274
01:02:31.520 --> 01:02:35.020
First, he's going to smile really big the whole time.
首先，他全程都要笑得特别灿烂。

1275
01:02:35.240 --> 01:02:35.600
Yep.
没错。

1276
01:02:35.600 --> 01:02:38.840
And the producer's like, what are you doing?
制片人问他，你在干什么？

1277
01:02:39.000 --> 01:02:39.640
Why are you smiling?
你为什么要笑？

1278
01:02:40.040 --> 01:02:44.980
And then the director's like, just do it like you're doing like a news anchor.
然后导演说，就像新闻主播那样演就行。

1279
01:02:45.260 --> 01:02:46.620
You know, like you're telling your news.
你知道，就像你在播报新闻一样。

1280
01:02:46.620 --> 01:02:47.600
You're delivering the news.
你在传达新闻。

1281
01:02:47.860 --> 01:02:48.580
Say it straight.
直白地说出来。

1282
01:02:48.960 --> 01:02:50.440
Oh, my gosh, lady.
天哪，女士。

1283
01:02:50.440 --> 01:02:55.480
And that's when we get Ed Helms doing Tom Brokaw.
然后我们就看到了艾德·赫尔姆斯模仿汤姆·布罗考。

1284
01:02:56.100 --> 01:02:56.600
Finally.
终于。

1285
01:02:57.260 --> 01:02:57.760
Amazing.
太棒了。

1286
01:02:58.060 --> 01:03:02.180
It makes it on the show what he's been doing behind the scenes for us all these years.
这把他多年来在幕后为我们做的事情展现到了节目上。

1287
01:03:02.460 --> 01:03:02.780
Yes.
是的。

1288
01:03:03.020 --> 01:03:04.820
This bit that we all loved.
这个我们大家都喜欢的段子。

1289
01:03:05.220 --> 01:03:07.960
And lady, I had to play it.
女士，我必须得放出来。

1290
01:03:08.120 --> 01:03:08.960
We have to hear it.
我们必须听听。

1291
01:03:09.160 --> 01:03:09.740
Let's hear it.
让我们听听吧。

1292
01:03:09.740 --> 01:03:16.000
This video is to demonstrate the HBRDC chemical handling protocols.
本视频旨在演示HBRDC化学品处理规程。

1293
01:03:16.620 --> 01:03:17.640
This is Tom Brokaw.
这是汤姆·布罗考。

1294
01:03:17.800 --> 01:03:18.500
It's a newscaster.
这是个新闻主播。

1295
01:03:18.640 --> 01:03:18.900
Come on.
拜托。

1296
01:03:19.000 --> 01:03:19.360
Who is it?
他是谁？

1297
01:03:19.500 --> 01:03:20.260
Tom Brokaw.
汤姆·布罗考。

1298
01:03:21.220 --> 01:03:23.260
And Daryl's look behind.
还有达里尔在后面的表情。

1299
01:03:23.500 --> 01:03:24.100
I know.
我知道。

1300
01:03:24.360 --> 01:03:25.580
He's like, oh, man.
他就像在说，天哪。

1301
01:03:25.580 --> 01:03:32.100
I wanted to mention that the other gentleman in these scenes playing the director is John Phillips.
我想提一下，这些场景里饰演导演的那位男士是约翰·菲利普斯。

1302
01:03:32.600 --> 01:03:39.340
He recently co-wrote the film No Hard Feelings, which was directed by our very own Gene Stepnitsky.
他最近参与编剧了电影《珍爱硬币》，该片由我们自己的吉恩·斯泰普尼茨基执导。

1303
01:03:39.620 --> 01:03:42.520
It was also produced by my manager, Naomi Odenkirk.
它也是由我的经纪人娜奥米·奥登科克制作的。

1304
01:03:42.740 --> 01:03:47.740
And Jennifer Lawrence was nominated for a Golden Globe for her performance in this movie in 2024.
詹妮弗·劳伦斯还凭借在这部电影中的表演获得了2024年金球奖提名。

1305
01:03:47.740 --> 01:03:51.640
It also won the People's Choice Award for Comedy Movie of the Year.
它还获得了人民选择奖年度喜剧电影奖。

1306
01:03:51.960 --> 01:03:52.540
Nice.
不错。

1307
01:03:52.980 --> 01:03:53.540
I know.
我知道。

1308
01:03:53.540 --> 01:03:58.800
And also, finally, for this scene, I have to read this fan catch from Tom F.
另外，最后，关于这一幕，我必须读一下汤姆·F发来的粉丝发现。

1309
01:03:58.980 --> 01:04:00.380
in Wolverhampton, UK.
他来自英国伍尔弗汉普顿。

1310
01:04:00.720 --> 01:04:09.220
Because Tom said, I have been waiting and waiting and waiting and waiting to submit this from the first episodes of your wonderful podcaSt.
因为汤姆说，我从你们精彩播客的第一集开始，就一直在等啊等啊等啊等，想提交这个发现。

1311
01:04:10.300 --> 01:04:12.380
Tom spotted a continuity thing.
汤姆发现了一个连贯性问题。

1312
01:04:12.540 --> 01:04:17.220
And Tom said, I haven't spotted a single other thing, unlike many of your other contributors.
汤姆说，不像你们的其他许多投稿人，我还没发现过任何其他问题。

1313
01:04:17.780 --> 01:04:21.740
So I'm really hoping that I'm the person who saw this one.
所以我真的希望我是发现这个问题的人。

1314
01:04:21.740 --> 01:04:22.820
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1315
01:04:22.900 --> 01:04:23.520
What is it?
是什么？

1316
01:04:23.960 --> 01:04:24.980
Here's what he saw.
这就是他看到的。

1317
01:04:25.640 --> 01:04:33.000
Tom says, when being filmed, Andy repeatedly calls the company HPRDC.
汤姆说，在拍摄时，安迪反复把公司称为HPRDC。

1318
01:04:33.000 --> 01:04:39.040
But the company badge that he's wearing says HRPDC.
但他佩戴的公司徽章上写的是HRPDC。

1319
01:04:39.480 --> 01:04:44.480
So Andy is getting the letters wrong when he speaks.
所以安迪在说话时把字母搞错了。

1320
01:04:45.340 --> 01:04:50.180
Tom said, is this Ed misreading the script?
汤姆问，这是埃德读错了剧本吗？

1321
01:04:50.180 --> 01:04:54.540
Or did the props and graphics department create the wrong label?
还是道具和图形部门制作了错误的标签？

1322
01:04:54.540 --> 01:04:57.580
Or was it scripted that he say it wrong?
又或者是剧本里就写着让他说错？

1323
01:04:57.880 --> 01:05:00.180
Well, that is a fantastic question.
嗯，这真是个绝妙的问题。

1324
01:05:00.260 --> 01:05:02.620
Well, Tom, I'm going to the shooting draft.
好吧，汤姆，我要去查查拍摄底稿。

1325
01:05:02.820 --> 01:05:05.240
And here is how it read in the shooting draft.
拍摄底稿上是这样写的。

1326
01:05:05.740 --> 01:05:13.400
Andy was supposed to say, this video is to demonstrate the HPRDC chemical handling protocol.
安迪本应说，这段视频是为了演示HPRDC化学品处理规程。

1327
01:05:13.400 --> 01:05:18.960
Okay, so I don't know why his badge says HRPDC.
好吧，所以我不知道为什么他的徽章上写的是HRPDC。

1328
01:05:19.560 --> 01:05:21.000
Which one is correct?
哪个才是正确的？

1329
01:05:21.340 --> 01:05:22.400
We don't know.
我们不知道。

1330
01:05:23.360 --> 01:05:25.180
Did we get to the bottom of it?
我们查清真相了吗？

1331
01:05:25.280 --> 01:05:26.640
Or did we mom detective it?
还是我们像妈妈侦探一样查了？

1332
01:05:27.020 --> 01:05:29.540
I think we mom detectived this one.
我想我们这次确实像妈妈侦探一样查了。

1333
01:05:29.800 --> 01:05:33.820
We confirmed that Ed said his line correctly.
我们确认了埃德说台词时是正确的。

1334
01:05:34.180 --> 01:05:34.720
Yes.
是的。

1335
01:05:34.720 --> 01:05:37.920
And we know that the badge doesn't match the line.
我们也知道徽章和台词对不上。

1336
01:05:37.920 --> 01:05:42.860
But we don't know if it was a mistake or we'll never know.
但我们不知道这是否是个错误，或者我们永远也不会知道了。

1337
01:05:43.020 --> 01:05:43.840
We'll never know.
我们永远也不会知道了。

1338
01:05:44.080 --> 01:05:44.840
We tried, Tom.
我们尽力了，汤姆。

1339
01:05:45.740 --> 01:05:49.120
Back in the warehouse, next up is Clark versus Aaron.
回到仓库，接下来是克拉克对阵亚伦。

1340
01:05:50.320 --> 01:05:52.340
Aaron's plane flies so far.
亚伦的飞机飞得好远。

1341
01:05:52.460 --> 01:05:53.620
She's really pumped.
她真的很兴奋。

1342
01:05:53.800 --> 01:05:59.200
And then she goes at Clark really hard, calling him piggy, oinking in his face.
然后她对克拉克发起了猛烈攻击，叫他小猪，还对着他的脸学猪叫。

1343
01:05:59.660 --> 01:06:03.120
Even Pete is like, Aaron, you need to relax.
连皮特都说，亚伦，你得冷静点。

1344
01:06:03.120 --> 01:06:07.220
And Clark is like, we still got to work together, so.
克拉克则说，我们还得一起工作，所以。

1345
01:06:07.720 --> 01:06:08.060
Yeah.
是啊。

1346
01:06:09.640 --> 01:06:10.560
You know what?
你知道吗？

1347
01:06:10.820 --> 01:06:13.180
There was even more in deleted scenes.
删减片段里还有更多内容。

1348
01:06:13.420 --> 01:06:18.220
Aaron would have yelled off camera, let's get this cotton picking show on the road, mother
亚伦本会在镜头外大喊，让我们赶紧开始这该死的表演吧，你这

1349
01:06:18.220 --> 01:06:18.740
f***er.
混蛋。

1350
01:06:19.300 --> 01:06:20.180
Oh, boy.
天哪。

1351
01:06:20.480 --> 01:06:20.740
Yeah.
是啊。

1352
01:06:21.740 --> 01:06:22.260
Scripted.
有剧本的。

1353
01:06:22.440 --> 01:06:22.960
Shot.
拍出来的。

1354
01:06:23.120 --> 01:06:23.360
Wow.
哇。

1355
01:06:23.660 --> 01:06:23.840
Yeah.
是啊。

1356
01:06:23.960 --> 01:06:24.220
Wow.
哇。

1357
01:06:24.580 --> 01:06:27.180
They were really showing Aaron's competitive side.
他们真的展现了亚伦好胜的一面。

1358
01:06:27.380 --> 01:06:32.060
And they were also clocking the fact that Pete was like, what is going on?
而且他们也注意到了皮特那种“到底发生了什么”的表情。

1359
01:06:32.060 --> 01:06:34.720
Well, Phyllis and Dwight are up next.
好了，接下来是菲利斯和德怀特。

1360
01:06:35.020 --> 01:06:36.420
Angela heckles Phyllis.
安吉拉在台下起哄菲利斯。

1361
01:06:36.700 --> 01:06:37.640
Dwight wins.
德怀特赢了。

1362
01:06:37.900 --> 01:06:39.160
Angela's very happy.
安吉拉非常高兴。

1363
01:06:39.580 --> 01:06:41.400
But, ooh, plot twiSt.
但是，噢，剧情反转了。

1364
01:06:41.740 --> 01:06:42.920
Esther has arrived.
埃丝特来了。

1365
01:06:43.160 --> 01:06:43.560
Yeah.
是啊。

1366
01:06:43.840 --> 01:06:44.940
Esther has arrived.
埃丝特来了。

1367
01:06:45.260 --> 01:06:47.000
Full of energy.
活力满满。

1368
01:06:47.000 --> 01:06:51.080
And she runs over to Dwight, gives him a big victory kiss.
她跑向德怀特，给了他一个大大的胜利之吻。

1369
01:06:51.600 --> 01:06:53.360
Angela's not happy about that.
安吉拉对此很不高兴。

1370
01:06:53.580 --> 01:06:58.080
She says she plucked the chickens extra fast so she could come support him.
她说她特意加快速度拔完鸡毛，就是为了赶来支持他。

1371
01:06:58.080 --> 01:07:02.480
We got a lot of fan questions, Angela, about the paper airplanes.
安吉拉，我们收到了很多粉丝关于纸飞机的提问。

1372
01:07:02.720 --> 01:07:06.140
We're going to get into a lot of scenes now of the paper airplane throwing.
我们现在要进入很多纸飞机投掷的场景了。

1373
01:07:06.520 --> 01:07:11.160
People wanted to know, were the paper airplanes photoshopped?
大家想知道，纸飞机是后期合成的吗？

1374
01:07:11.880 --> 01:07:13.080
And Jenny M.
还有来自德克萨斯州凯蒂的珍妮·M问，

1375
01:07:13.300 --> 01:07:17.720
from Katy, Texas said, did Phil Shea have to make all those paper airplanes?
菲尔·谢是不是得制作所有那些纸飞机？

1376
01:07:17.920 --> 01:07:18.800
Were they CGI?
它们是电脑特效吗？

1377
01:07:19.320 --> 01:07:20.940
Did we throw them ourselves?
是我们自己扔的吗？

1378
01:07:21.520 --> 01:07:22.800
How was this done?
这是怎么做到的？

1379
01:07:23.560 --> 01:07:30.140
Well, I can tell you, I remembered immediately when I rewatched this, I even called you about
嗯，我可以告诉你，重温这一集时我立刻就想起来了，我甚至还为此给你打过电话，

1380
01:07:30.140 --> 01:07:30.500
it, Jenna.
珍娜。

1381
01:07:30.720 --> 01:07:35.640
I was like, remember the professional paper airplane fellas they brought in?
我说，还记得他们请来的那些专业纸飞机高手吗？

1382
01:07:35.840 --> 01:07:38.500
These guys came and made these airplanes.
这些人来了，制作了这些飞机。

1383
01:07:38.860 --> 01:07:41.060
They were works of art, really.
它们真的是艺术品。

1384
01:07:41.300 --> 01:07:45.900
And I'm going to point out later the moment where mine actually went far because my real
我稍后会指出我那架飞机飞得很远的那一刻，因为我当时真实的

1385
01:07:45.900 --> 01:07:47.420
reaction is very honeSt.
反应非常诚实。

1386
01:07:47.420 --> 01:07:49.420
But yeah, I remember these guys.
但没错，我记得这些人。

1387
01:07:49.620 --> 01:07:51.300
They were set up in the warehouse.
他们在仓库里布置好了。

1388
01:07:51.300 --> 01:07:52.820
They had folded all these planes.
他们折好了所有这些飞机。

1389
01:07:53.060 --> 01:07:56.220
They did show us kind of this arm motion to make.
他们确实给我们演示了那种投掷的手臂动作。

1390
01:07:56.420 --> 01:08:00.020
You can see the people that win kind of have a similar arm motion, you know?
你可以看到获胜的人动作都差不多，你知道吧？

1391
01:08:00.700 --> 01:08:00.780
Yep.
没错。

1392
01:08:00.920 --> 01:08:04.040
Dwight and Angela and Aaron, we kind of throw them the same way.
德怀特、安吉拉还有亚伦，我们投掷的方式都差不多。

1393
01:08:04.300 --> 01:08:09.140
So I know there were real paper airplanes, but I also know they had to zhuzh it a little
所以我知道那是真的纸飞机，但我也知道他们在剪辑时

1394
01:08:09.140 --> 01:08:09.980
in editing.
稍微润色了一下。

1395
01:08:10.380 --> 01:08:10.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1396
01:08:10.700 --> 01:08:13.800
I mean, the answer is they're not CGI airplanes.
我的意思是，答案是它们不是电脑特效飞机。

1397
01:08:14.020 --> 01:08:14.720
They're all real.
它们都是真的。

1398
01:08:14.980 --> 01:08:15.160
Yeah.
是啊。

1399
01:08:15.320 --> 01:08:18.080
And, you know, the cast members are really throwing them.
而且，你知道，演员们确实是在亲自投掷。

1400
01:08:18.280 --> 01:08:24.180
If you ever see an airplane going somewhere and it's just the airplane, that was probably
如果你看到飞机飞向某个地方，画面里只有飞机，那大概就是

1401
01:08:24.180 --> 01:08:29.780
thrown by someone else, one of the professionals, you know, so that it would hit a certain mark.
由专业人士扔出的，你知道，这样它才能击中特定的目标。

1402
01:08:30.220 --> 01:08:32.460
But it was a lot of fun.
但那真的很有趣。

1403
01:08:32.660 --> 01:08:36.500
I mean, it's fun to throw a paper airplane that you know is good.
我是说，扔出一架你知道性能很好的纸飞机很有意思。

1404
01:08:36.800 --> 01:08:37.640
It is.
确实。

1405
01:08:37.640 --> 01:08:42.760
And, you know, I don't know if you remember this, Jenna, but we all made a paper airplane
而且，你知道，我不知道你还记不记得，珍娜，我们当时都自己做了纸飞机，

1406
01:08:42.760 --> 01:08:48.060
ourselves and I threw my paper airplane and it went nowhere.
我扔出了我的纸飞机，结果它根本飞不动。

1407
01:08:48.420 --> 01:08:50.060
It's like nose dived.
就像一头栽了下去。

1408
01:08:50.280 --> 01:08:54.660
And then I threw one of the ones they made and it was like astonishing.
然后我扔了他们做的一架，简直惊人。

1409
01:08:55.020 --> 01:08:58.500
It flew almost the whole entire length of the warehouse.
它几乎飞过了整个仓库的长度。

1410
01:08:58.740 --> 01:09:01.780
In fact, I feel like they had to tone it down a little.
事实上，我觉得他们不得不稍微收敛一点。

1411
01:09:01.940 --> 01:09:03.680
They're like, make them not go so far, guys.
他们说，伙计们，别让它飞那么远。

1412
01:09:03.840 --> 01:09:04.880
You're making them too good.
你们把它做得太好了。

1413
01:09:05.320 --> 01:09:05.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1414
01:09:06.160 --> 01:09:06.700
All right.
好吧。

1415
01:09:06.700 --> 01:09:09.040
Next up, let's go to Andy's eyeball.
接下来，让我们看看安迪的眼球。

1416
01:09:09.860 --> 01:09:10.120
Yeah.
没错。

1417
01:09:10.980 --> 01:09:17.320
Andy's going to find out that the next scene requires him to hold his eyelids open and flesh
安迪即将发现下一场戏需要他睁大眼睑，并瞪大双眼，

1418
01:09:17.320 --> 01:09:22.280
out his eyes as a way of demonstrating what happens if you get a chemical in your eye.
以此来演示如果眼睛进了化学物质会发生什么。

1419
01:09:22.420 --> 01:09:24.380
You have to use the eyewash station.
你必须使用洗眼台。

1420
01:09:24.600 --> 01:09:29.000
And we should say he didn't have to have any chemicals put in his eye.
我们得说明一下，他的眼睛里并没有真的被滴入任何化学物质。

1421
01:09:29.120 --> 01:09:31.320
He was simply just going to rinse his eyes out with water.
他只是要用清水冲洗眼睛而已。

1422
01:09:31.320 --> 01:09:37.040
Yes, but Andy does not like eye stuff.
是的，但安迪不喜欢眼睛相关的东西。

1423
01:09:37.280 --> 01:09:43.260
There was a scene earlier where he's confronted with Toby's gooey eye and he can't even take it.
之前有一场戏，他面对托比那只粘糊糊的眼睛时，甚至都受不了。

1424
01:09:43.480 --> 01:09:45.940
He's not comfortable doing his own stunts.
他不习惯亲自做特技动作。

1425
01:09:46.820 --> 01:09:51.840
He wonders if there's going to be CGI water that they're going to add in later.
他想知道之后会不会用电脑特效加上水。

1426
01:09:52.060 --> 01:09:55.340
And they're like, no, you just have to do this.
而他们说，不，你必须亲自做。

1427
01:09:55.820 --> 01:09:59.460
Well, in the episode, we're going to go back to the paper airplane conteSt.
嗯，在这一集中，我们要回到纸飞机大赛。

1428
01:09:59.640 --> 01:10:02.360
But why don't we stay here with Andy and his eyes?
但为什么我们不先留在这里看看安迪和他的眼睛呢？

1429
01:10:02.940 --> 01:10:09.000
Well, you know, Halstead shared with us that they knew Ed was great at physical comedy and freaking out.
嗯，你知道，霍尔斯特德告诉我们，他们知道艾德非常擅长肢体喜剧和表现惊慌失措。

1430
01:10:09.300 --> 01:10:18.920
You know, in the episode he and Warren wrote Cafe Disco, there's this scene at the end where Kelly starts to pierce Andy's ear and he starts to yell and they cut away.
你知道，在他和沃伦合写的《咖啡迪斯科》那一集中，结尾有一场戏，凯莉开始给安迪穿耳洞，他开始尖叫，然后镜头就切走了。

1431
01:10:19.100 --> 01:10:23.660
So they knew that Ed playing Andy freaked out was going to be a home run.
所以他们知道，让艾德扮演惊慌失措的安迪绝对会大获成功。

1432
01:10:24.360 --> 01:10:24.920
Nice.
不错。

1433
01:10:25.500 --> 01:10:28.940
Well, we got some fan questions about the eyewash scene.
我们收到了一些粉丝关于洗眼戏份的问题。

1434
01:10:28.940 --> 01:10:35.240
Evie L from Texas said, did Ed Helms really put his eye in the eyewash?
来自德克萨斯州的伊薇·L问，艾德·赫尔姆斯真的把眼睛放进洗眼器里了吗？

1435
01:10:35.980 --> 01:10:38.000
The answer is yes.
答案是肯定的。

1436
01:10:38.440 --> 01:10:38.600
Yeah.
是的。

1437
01:10:39.700 --> 01:10:42.360
Steve Burgess said this was a real eyewash station.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯说这是一个真正的洗眼台。

1438
01:10:42.580 --> 01:10:49.300
We changed the signage to avoid any clearance issues, but that's what they look like.
我们更改了标识以避免任何版权问题，但它们看起来就是那样。

1439
01:10:49.440 --> 01:10:54.480
And our special effects guys fed it water that was a distilled sterile water.
我们的特效人员给它输送的是蒸馏过的无菌水。

1440
01:10:54.480 --> 01:10:57.000
So they knew that it would be safe for Ed.
所以他们知道这对艾德来说是安全的。

1441
01:10:57.000 --> 01:10:59.240
But he really did it.
但他确实亲自做了。

1442
01:10:59.560 --> 01:11:01.140
And it's so funny.
而且太搞笑了。

1443
01:11:01.400 --> 01:11:07.700
I mean, Daryl is there and Andy puts his face into this water and the whole time he is screaming.
我是说，达里尔就在旁边，安迪把脸埋进水里，全程都在尖叫。

1444
01:11:08.200 --> 01:11:10.780
And then he sits up and they're like, that was great.
然后他坐起来，他们说，太棒了。

1445
01:11:10.780 --> 01:11:13.140
We can take out the screams and poSt.
我们可以在后期把尖叫声去掉。

1446
01:11:14.160 --> 01:11:16.060
So, so good.
真是太棒了。

1447
01:11:16.500 --> 01:11:17.360
I know.
我知道。

1448
01:11:17.480 --> 01:11:18.460
He's so funny.
他太搞笑了。

1449
01:11:18.880 --> 01:11:20.760
And Carla is very pleased.
而且卡拉非常满意。

1450
01:11:21.340 --> 01:11:23.720
Carla is like, kid can act.
卡拉说，这孩子真会演戏。

1451
01:11:24.180 --> 01:11:25.660
Loved that line too.
我也很喜欢那句台词。

1452
01:11:25.660 --> 01:11:26.640
Me too.
我也是。

1453
01:11:26.640 --> 01:11:26.720
Me too.
我也是。

1454
01:11:27.220 --> 01:11:28.700
The kid can act.
这孩子挺会演的。

1455
01:11:28.960 --> 01:11:29.840
Get him a chair.
给他搬把椅子。

1456
01:11:30.360 --> 01:11:30.840
Yeah.
是啊。

1457
01:11:31.100 --> 01:11:32.460
My actors sit.
我的演员得坐着。

1458
01:11:34.340 --> 01:11:38.260
Well, now it's time for Toby and Angela to face off.
好了，现在轮到托比和安吉拉对决了。

1459
01:11:38.680 --> 01:11:42.240
Angela's going to go first and has a fantastic throw.
安吉拉先来，她投得非常棒。

1460
01:11:42.240 --> 01:11:48.140
And if you go to 12 minutes and 39 seconds, that sort of yelp slash squeal that I make,
如果你看到12分39秒，我发出的那种尖叫声，

1461
01:11:48.220 --> 01:11:53.960
I'm like, is real because I was so excited because I got to use one of those professional
我是说，那是真的，因为我太兴奋了，因为我终于能用上那种专业的

1462
01:11:53.960 --> 01:11:55.700
paper airplanes and it went really far.
纸飞机了，而且它飞得特别远。

1463
01:11:55.900 --> 01:11:56.860
That's my real reaction.
那是我的真实反应。

1464
01:11:57.060 --> 01:11:57.960
I really threw that.
那确实是我投的。

1465
01:11:58.080 --> 01:11:59.320
And that's where it landed.
那就是它落下的地方。

1466
01:11:59.720 --> 01:12:03.680
Well, I couldn't help but notice how long your plane stayed in the air.
我忍不住注意到你的飞机在空中停留了多久。

1467
01:12:03.840 --> 01:12:06.280
And it's about 4.5 seconds.
大约有4.5秒。

1468
01:12:06.280 --> 01:12:07.500
Thank you.
谢谢。

1469
01:12:08.040 --> 01:12:11.460
I mean, I should say thank you, professional paper airplane people.
我是说，我应该谢谢那些专业玩纸飞机的人。

1470
01:12:11.920 --> 01:12:18.540
Well, I'll have you know that in addition to a contest for how far your plane can go,
我得让你知道，除了比谁的飞机飞得远，

1471
01:12:18.740 --> 01:12:22.520
there's also a world record for the longest flight time.
还有一个飞行时间最长的世界纪录。

1472
01:12:22.900 --> 01:12:25.860
So how long it stays in the air.
也就是它在空中停留的时间。

1473
01:12:26.040 --> 01:12:27.480
That makes sense to me.
这对我来说很有道理。

1474
01:12:27.480 --> 01:12:31.920
And that record is currently held by Takua Toda from Japan.
目前的纪录保持者是日本的户田拓夫。

1475
01:12:31.940 --> 01:12:34.740
It was set in December 2010.
那是2010年12月创下的。

1476
01:12:35.660 --> 01:12:41.440
And this paper plane stayed in the air for 29.2 seconds.
那架纸飞机在空中停留了29.2秒。

1477
01:12:42.820 --> 01:12:43.460
Wow.
哇。

1478
01:12:43.620 --> 01:12:47.880
At first, I thought you were going to say 29 minutes and I was about to fall out of my chair.
起初我还以为你要说29分钟，我差点从椅子上掉下来。

1479
01:12:48.200 --> 01:12:48.820
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1480
01:12:48.820 --> 01:12:49.180
My goodness.
天哪。

1481
01:12:49.560 --> 01:12:50.700
I was like, what?
我当时心想，什么？

1482
01:12:51.920 --> 01:12:53.360
That's impressive though.
不过那确实很厉害。

1483
01:12:53.680 --> 01:12:54.200
Yes.
是的。

1484
01:12:54.760 --> 01:12:57.940
But, I mean, to get a sense of how long that plane flew,
但是，我是说，为了让你感受一下那架飞机飞了多久，

1485
01:12:58.120 --> 01:13:00.520
if you're watching this scene and you're watching Angela's airplane,
如果你在看这一幕，看着安吉拉的纸飞机，

1486
01:13:00.820 --> 01:13:04.040
imagine if that scene went on five times longer.
想象一下如果那一幕持续的时间是现在的五倍。

1487
01:13:04.420 --> 01:13:09.060
It's almost the same amount of time that Jim and Pam were silent on Boo's Cruise.
那几乎和吉姆和帕姆在“Boo's Cruise”那集里沉默的时间一样长。

1488
01:13:09.500 --> 01:13:10.260
That's right.
没错。

1489
01:13:10.440 --> 01:13:11.920
That was like 21 seconds.
那大概有21秒。

1490
01:13:12.560 --> 01:13:12.900
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1491
01:13:13.080 --> 01:13:13.920
It's longer.
更长一些。

1492
01:13:14.160 --> 01:13:18.240
It's the longest airplane flew longer than Jim and Pam's moment of silence.
那架纸飞机的飞行时间比吉姆和帕姆沉默的那一刻还要长。

1493
01:13:18.500 --> 01:13:18.700
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1494
01:13:20.080 --> 01:13:22.480
Oh, I hope we didn't ruin that scene for people.
噢，希望我们没有毁了那一幕。

1495
01:13:22.480 --> 01:13:27.540
Now, when they go back to watch that, they're going to imagine a paper airplane flying through
现在他们回去重看那一幕时，脑子里会浮现出一架纸飞机飞过

1496
01:13:27.540 --> 01:13:28.040
the air.
空中的画面。

1497
01:13:28.460 --> 01:13:28.960
Sorry.
抱歉。

1498
01:13:30.900 --> 01:13:31.760
Here's the thing.
问题是这样的。

1499
01:13:31.900 --> 01:13:36.660
With Jenna and I doing this rewatch and watching these episodes so many times, it's the office
我和珍娜在做这次重温，看了这么多遍剧集，办公室

1500
01:13:36.660 --> 01:13:38.580
just lives in us now.
已经融入我们的生活了。

1501
01:13:38.920 --> 01:13:40.180
It lives in my brain.
它就在我脑子里挥之不去。

1502
01:13:40.640 --> 01:13:42.580
We relate everything back to like an episode.
我们把一切都和某集剧情联系起来。

1503
01:13:42.580 --> 01:13:44.920
We were probably so annoying to be around.
我们那时候在别人眼里肯定特别烦人。

1504
01:13:44.920 --> 01:13:49.380
Well, it's Toby's turn now, and he's just already defeated.
好了，现在轮到托比了，他还没开始就已经认输了。

1505
01:13:49.600 --> 01:13:53.500
He just crumples it up, and he bails, basically.
他把纸团一揉，基本上就直接放弃了。

1506
01:13:53.800 --> 01:13:54.840
So Angela wins.
所以安吉拉赢了。

1507
01:13:55.060 --> 01:13:56.060
Dwight applauds.
德怀特鼓掌。

1508
01:13:56.300 --> 01:13:57.560
He's very happy.
他非常高兴。

1509
01:13:57.780 --> 01:13:59.400
And Esther clocks this.
埃丝特注意到了这一点。

1510
01:13:59.700 --> 01:14:02.940
She says, why are we happy for that little woman?
她说，我们为什么要为那个小个子女人高兴？

1511
01:14:03.660 --> 01:14:09.320
And then Dwight says, you know, I pity her because she could have had everything, and she lost
然后德怀特说，你知道吗，我同情她，因为她本可以拥有一切，但她却失去

1512
01:14:09.320 --> 01:14:09.800
it all.
了一切。

1513
01:14:10.500 --> 01:14:10.780
Yeah.
没错。

1514
01:14:11.180 --> 01:14:15.920
And now we're going to see Dwight face off against Erin, and guess who wins?
现在我们要看德怀特和艾琳对决，猜猜谁赢了？

1515
01:14:17.140 --> 01:14:17.700
Dwight!
德怀特！

1516
01:14:18.720 --> 01:14:20.640
Ellie Kemper's reaction to losing.
艾丽·坎伯输掉比赛后的反应。

1517
01:14:21.720 --> 01:14:28.860
I had to watch this scene over and over and over when she kicks that box, and her foot
我把这一幕看了又看，看了又看，她踢那个盒子的时候，脚

1518
01:14:28.860 --> 01:14:32.540
gets stuck, and then she loses her shoe in all the popcorn.
卡住了，然后鞋子掉进了爆米花里。

1519
01:14:32.960 --> 01:14:33.520
Yes.
是的。

1520
01:14:33.840 --> 01:14:35.460
It was so funny.
太搞笑了。

1521
01:14:35.720 --> 01:14:37.540
And she's just like, I'm just really mad right now.
她当时就像是，我现在真的特别生气。

1522
01:14:37.540 --> 01:14:38.900
I'm just really mad right now.
我现在真的特别生气。

1523
01:14:39.200 --> 01:14:40.140
I'm angry.
我很愤怒。

1524
01:14:40.580 --> 01:14:43.320
And like, clearly, that wasn't supposed to happen.
显然，那不是预料之中的事。

1525
01:14:43.580 --> 01:14:46.120
I don't think her foot was meant to break that box.
我觉得她的脚本来不该踢破那个盒子的。

1526
01:14:46.280 --> 01:14:48.140
I don't think she was meant to lose her shoe.
我觉得她本来不该把鞋子弄丢的。

1527
01:14:48.300 --> 01:14:50.720
And the two of them hold it together so well.
他们两个都演得特别好，没笑场。

1528
01:14:50.900 --> 01:14:51.840
It's beautiful.
太精彩了。

1529
01:14:52.140 --> 01:14:53.120
It is.
确实。

1530
01:14:53.260 --> 01:14:58.240
And I just loved what Warren and Halstead shared with us about how important this story
我特别喜欢沃伦和霍尔斯特德分享的内容，关于这个故事对于艾琳和皮特的感情有多重要，

1531
01:14:58.240 --> 01:15:03.900
is for the Erin and Pete relationship that Pete is now starting to question it.
皮特现在开始质疑这段关系了。

1532
01:15:03.900 --> 01:15:07.380
He's like, maybe we're not the right fit.
他觉得，也许我们并不合适。

1533
01:15:08.020 --> 01:15:13.780
Well, they said they were starting to think that Pete and Erin would not end up together.
嗯，他们说他们开始觉得皮特和艾琳最终不会在一起了。

1534
01:15:13.960 --> 01:15:14.320
Yes.
是的。

1535
01:15:14.700 --> 01:15:18.600
And so they had to show a way that maybe they weren't compatible.
所以他们必须展示出一种方式，说明他们可能并不兼容。

1536
01:15:18.900 --> 01:15:19.480
That's right.
没错。

1537
01:15:20.180 --> 01:15:24.000
Well, now we're back at Jim and Pam and Clark's desk clump.
好了，现在回到吉姆、帕姆和克拉克的办公桌区域。

1538
01:15:24.260 --> 01:15:28.500
And Jim and Pam are continuing to speak in their therapy speak.
吉姆和帕姆继续用他们的心理咨询术语对话。

1539
01:15:28.500 --> 01:15:31.620
And it's becoming more passive aggressive.
而且变得越来越阴阳怪气了。

1540
01:15:32.240 --> 01:15:35.480
And Clark is like, hey, are you guys high?
克拉克就问，嘿，你们俩是不是嗑嗨了？

1541
01:15:35.600 --> 01:15:38.180
Because if you're high, can you pass me some?
如果你们嗨了，能不能分我点？

1542
01:15:38.480 --> 01:15:40.660
And they're like, no, we're not high.
他们回答说，不，我们没嗨。

1543
01:15:41.520 --> 01:15:41.680
Yeah.
没错。

1544
01:15:41.840 --> 01:15:45.040
This is when Pam is going to have her talking head where she says,
这就是帕姆对着镜头独白的时候，她说，

1545
01:15:45.220 --> 01:15:51.520
I just wish we'd started this exercise six months ago because my heart feels just blocked
我真希望我们六个月前就开始做这个练习，因为我现在感觉心里

1546
01:15:51.520 --> 01:15:52.320
up right now.
堵得慌。

1547
01:15:52.920 --> 01:15:53.220
Yeah.
没错。

1548
01:15:53.220 --> 01:15:56.040
I felt that when she said it.
她说这话的时候我感同身受。

1549
01:15:56.120 --> 01:15:56.700
I felt it.
我也有同感。

1550
01:15:56.980 --> 01:15:57.960
I did too.
我也是。

1551
01:15:58.520 --> 01:16:01.620
I want you to know that there was more to this talking head.
我想让你知道，这段采访片段还有更多内容。

1552
01:16:02.080 --> 01:16:07.960
She would have gone on to say, I want to believe talking like robots will help.
她本来还会接着说，我想相信像机器人一样说话会有所帮助。

1553
01:16:08.080 --> 01:16:11.820
Although robots aren't really known for their emotional connections.
虽然机器人并不以情感交流而闻名。

1554
01:16:12.480 --> 01:16:14.460
And are you ready for this, Angela?
安吉拉，你准备好了吗？

1555
01:16:14.880 --> 01:16:16.480
No, I'm not.
不，我没准备好。

1556
01:16:16.860 --> 01:16:18.940
This is what Pam would have said next.
这就是帕姆接下来本来会说的话。

1557
01:16:19.960 --> 01:16:24.160
Well, I guess R2-D2 and C-3PO were pretty attached.
好吧，我想R2-D2和C-3PO的感情还是挺深厚的。

1558
01:16:24.980 --> 01:16:26.480
Is that where we're headed?
我们是要往那个方向发展吗？

1559
01:16:27.240 --> 01:16:29.840
She would have made a Star Wars reference.
她本来会引用《星球大战》的梗。

1560
01:16:30.320 --> 01:16:30.500
Star Wars.
《星球大战》。

1561
01:16:30.700 --> 01:16:33.540
Star Wars and Lord of the Rings in one episode.
一集里既有《星球大战》又有《指环王》。

1562
01:16:33.580 --> 01:16:34.540
Come on.
得了吧。

1563
01:16:34.860 --> 01:16:35.480
I know.
我知道。

1564
01:16:35.540 --> 01:16:41.540
It looks like Pam and Angela could be bonding over their love of sci-fi filMs.
看来帕姆和安吉拉可能会因为对科幻电影的热爱而建立起联系。

1565
01:16:42.420 --> 01:16:44.120
That's a scene I want to see.
那是我很想看到的场景。

1566
01:16:44.340 --> 01:16:47.900
I want to see the two of them in the break room talking sci-fi.
我想看她们俩在休息室里谈论科幻片。

1567
01:16:47.900 --> 01:16:48.920
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1568
01:16:49.640 --> 01:16:52.340
Kevin is still working really hard on paper airplanes.
凯文还在非常努力地折纸飞机。

1569
01:16:52.520 --> 01:16:55.140
There is a whole table of airplanes.
桌子上放满了纸飞机。

1570
01:16:55.340 --> 01:16:56.780
And now he's gluing stuff.
现在他还在粘东西。

1571
01:16:56.780 --> 01:16:58.380
He's pasting things together.
他在把东西拼在一起。

1572
01:16:58.680 --> 01:17:00.120
It's such a mess.
简直乱成一团。

1573
01:17:00.260 --> 01:17:02.120
This is like crafting gone wrong.
这就像是手工制作翻车现场。

1574
01:17:02.680 --> 01:17:07.240
This scene is completely unnecessary for the plot of this episode.
这一幕对本集的剧情来说完全没必要。

1575
01:17:07.240 --> 01:17:09.920
But it is an absolute delight.
但它绝对是一种享受。

1576
01:17:10.080 --> 01:17:16.620
It is a display of beautiful comic timing, both physical and oral.
这展现了绝妙的喜剧时机，无论是肢体还是语言上。

1577
01:17:16.620 --> 01:17:18.340
Is that a type of comedy?
那是一种喜剧类型吗？

1578
01:17:18.640 --> 01:17:19.340
Oral comedy?
语言喜剧？

1579
01:17:19.560 --> 01:17:20.340
I guess it is.
我想应该是吧。

1580
01:17:20.840 --> 01:17:23.180
Anyway, all of his timing is beautiful.
总之，他所有的节奏把握都很棒。

1581
01:17:23.200 --> 01:17:25.040
I really enjoyed this moment.
我真的很喜欢这一刻。

1582
01:17:25.720 --> 01:17:28.120
It's now time for the final round.
现在是决赛轮的时间了。

1583
01:17:28.520 --> 01:17:30.260
It is Angela versus Dwight.
是安吉拉对阵德怀特。

1584
01:17:30.820 --> 01:17:33.040
Dwight had a talking head that was deleted.
德怀特有一段被删减的采访片段。

1585
01:17:33.040 --> 01:17:37.300
And he talks about why he doesn't need the money, but Angela does.
他在里面谈到了为什么他不需要这笔钱，而安吉拉需要。

1586
01:17:37.480 --> 01:17:38.540
And I thought you should hear it.
我觉得你应该听听。

1587
01:17:39.400 --> 01:17:40.520
I don't need this win.
我不需要这次胜利。

1588
01:17:40.700 --> 01:17:43.660
I've got a lucrative job, an enormous farm, and this building.
我有份高薪工作，一个巨大的农场，还有这栋楼。

1589
01:17:44.160 --> 01:17:50.420
Angela has nothing but a child who, while adorable, won't bring in revenue for another five or six years.
安吉拉除了一个孩子外一无所有，虽然孩子很可爱，但未来五六年内都不会带来任何收入。

1590
01:17:51.600 --> 01:17:52.860
That's so interesting.
那太有意思了。

1591
01:17:53.780 --> 01:17:58.380
It's very shrewd, isn't it, that he thinks Philip is going to be working in five years?
他认为菲利普五年后就能工作，这想法真是太精明了，不是吗？

1592
01:18:00.340 --> 01:18:03.040
It is, but he's, you know, yeah.
确实，但他，你知道的，嗯。

1593
01:18:03.260 --> 01:18:06.580
He has an interesting way of attaching value to things.
他衡量事物价值的方式很有趣。

1594
01:18:06.920 --> 01:18:09.440
Well, Angela's first throw is terrible.
好吧，安吉拉的第一投太糟糕了。

1595
01:18:10.040 --> 01:18:12.940
And then Dwight fumbles his on purpose.
然后德怀特故意搞砸了他的那一投。

1596
01:18:13.940 --> 01:18:14.920
Esther clocks this.
埃丝特注意到了这一点。

1597
01:18:15.120 --> 01:18:19.760
It's said in the script, Esther sees Dwight do this and is jealous.
剧本里写着，埃丝特看到德怀特这么做，感到很嫉妒。

1598
01:18:21.460 --> 01:18:23.600
Yes, that's what it said in the shooting draft.
是的，拍摄底稿上就是这么写的。

1599
01:18:23.900 --> 01:18:29.740
And then she goes over to Angela and she's very patronizing and says, you know, they want her to win.
然后她走到安吉拉身边，表现得非常傲慢，说，你知道的，他们想让她赢。

1600
01:18:29.920 --> 01:18:32.700
They know she needs this money, so use it wisely.
他们知道她需要这笔钱，所以要好好利用。

1601
01:18:33.000 --> 01:18:36.780
And then Esther strokes sort of the back of Angela's hair.
然后埃丝特摸了摸安吉拉的后脑勺。

1602
01:18:37.040 --> 01:18:38.340
That was not scripted.
那不是剧本里写的。

1603
01:18:38.540 --> 01:18:39.780
Nora improvised that.
那是诺拉即兴发挥的。

1604
01:18:39.980 --> 01:18:46.660
And then I reacted and improvised as Angela would react, which is horrified that this woman has touched her hair.
然后我做出了反应，以安吉拉会有的反应即兴表演，也就是对这个女人碰了她的头发感到惊恐。

1605
01:18:46.880 --> 01:18:48.200
It was so fun.
那太有趣了。

1606
01:18:48.200 --> 01:18:51.320
And when Nora did it, we were like, okay, you've got to keep doing that.
当诺拉那样做的时候，我们当时就想，好吧，你一定要继续那样做。

1607
01:18:51.560 --> 01:18:55.880
And then Angela goes over to Dwight and she says, do not tank this.
然后安吉拉走到德怀特身边说，别搞砸了。

1608
01:18:56.100 --> 01:18:57.700
Like, she doesn't want his pity.
她不想要他的同情。

1609
01:18:58.160 --> 01:19:01.760
Well, at first she's very delighted by the gesture.
嗯，起初她对这个举动感到非常高兴。

1610
01:19:01.760 --> 01:19:06.320
But when Esther gets involved, she's like, no, her pride comes out.
但当埃丝特介入时，她就觉得不行，她的自尊心上来了。

1611
01:19:06.520 --> 01:19:07.080
That's right.
没错。

1612
01:19:07.580 --> 01:19:11.280
Angela is going to go up to Dwight now and says, do not tank this throw.
安吉拉现在要走到德怀特身边说，别把这次投掷搞砸了。

1613
01:19:11.760 --> 01:19:14.120
And so he throws and it goes far.
于是他投了，而且投得很远。

1614
01:19:14.340 --> 01:19:16.640
And then she purposely tanks hers.
然后她故意把自己的那次投掷搞砸了。

1615
01:19:17.700 --> 01:19:19.140
I loved this moment.
我喜欢这个时刻。

1616
01:19:19.520 --> 01:19:25.760
Because Nora had improvised touching the back of my hair, we knew I had to touch her head somehow.
因为诺拉即兴摸了我的后脑勺，我们知道我必须得想办法摸摸她的头。

1617
01:19:26.020 --> 01:19:26.480
Yeah.
是啊。

1618
01:19:26.580 --> 01:19:28.260
But she's so much taller than me.
但她比我高太多了。

1619
01:19:28.680 --> 01:19:32.520
So Angela goes up to Esther and says, I guess you guys needed the money more than me.
所以安吉拉走到埃丝特身边说，我想你们比我更需要这笔钱。

1620
01:19:32.780 --> 01:19:34.080
And then I improvise.
然后我即兴发挥。

1621
01:19:34.240 --> 01:19:34.560
Huh.
呵。

1622
01:19:34.980 --> 01:19:36.020
Use it wisely.
好好利用它吧。

1623
01:19:36.020 --> 01:19:38.620
And I touched her forehead and hair.
然后我摸了摸她的额头和头发。

1624
01:19:39.160 --> 01:19:41.640
And I saunter off very pridefully.
然后我非常骄傲地大步走开了。

1625
01:19:42.200 --> 01:19:46.240
So that was a really fun back and forth that I got to have with Nora.
所以那是我和诺拉之间一次非常有趣的来回互动。

1626
01:19:46.460 --> 01:19:47.700
I love that she did that.
我喜欢她那样做。

1627
01:19:47.800 --> 01:19:49.580
And then I love that I got to have that response.
我也喜欢我能做出那样的回应。

1628
01:19:50.480 --> 01:19:51.900
Well, I loved this whole moment.
嗯，我喜欢整个这一幕。

1629
01:19:52.060 --> 01:19:53.620
I really didn't know what was going to happen.
我真的不知道会发生什么。

1630
01:19:53.860 --> 01:19:58.440
I didn't know if Dwight was going to find a way to let Angela win.
我不知道德怀特是否会想办法让安吉拉赢。

1631
01:19:58.440 --> 01:20:01.520
But all of it was just so in character for you guys.
但这一切对你们俩来说都太符合角色性格了。

1632
01:20:01.520 --> 01:20:03.440
And I think that's what I liked about it.
我想这就是我喜欢它的原因。

1633
01:20:03.680 --> 01:20:06.740
I also love Angela's talking head when she's like, you know what?
我也喜欢安吉拉的采访片段，她说，你知道吗？

1634
01:20:06.840 --> 01:20:08.260
Dwight showed weakness today.
德怀特今天表现出了软弱。

1635
01:20:08.580 --> 01:20:09.860
And I don't need it.
而我不需要它。

1636
01:20:09.900 --> 01:20:10.800
I don't need his pity.
我不需要他的同情。

1637
01:20:11.040 --> 01:20:12.380
I have my dignity.
我有我的尊严。

1638
01:20:12.380 --> 01:20:16.080
And as she's saying it, she's stealing all the toilet paper from the bathroom.
而且当她说这话时，她正在从洗手间偷走所有的卫生纸。

1639
01:20:16.580 --> 01:20:17.060
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1640
01:20:17.320 --> 01:20:22.020
It did say in the script that even as she walks out with all that toilet paper, she's holding her head high.
剧本里确实写了，即使在她抱着那一堆卫生纸走出来时，她依然昂着头。

1641
01:20:22.740 --> 01:20:24.200
Yes, I read that too.
是的，我也读到了。

1642
01:20:24.200 --> 01:20:27.600
Well, that's the end of our paper airplane storyline.
好了，我们的纸飞机剧情线到此结束。

1643
01:20:27.600 --> 01:20:39.360
And just to wrap things up, I thought y'all might like to know that the largest flying paper airplane is a 53-pound paper glider that flew 59 feet.
最后总结一下，我想你们可能会想知道，最大的飞行纸飞机是一架53磅重的纸质滑翔机，飞行了59英尺。

1644
01:20:39.800 --> 01:20:43.980
It has a wingspan of 60 feet, a length of 17 feet.
它的翼展为60英尺，长度为17英尺。

1645
01:20:44.280 --> 01:20:51.180
And it was constructed in Germany in 2013 by a team of 16 university students and employees.
它是由一个由16名大学生和员工组成的团队于2013年在德国建造的。

1646
01:20:51.880 --> 01:20:59.540
A larger paper airplane was built in Fitchburg, USA in 2018, but it was not able to fly.
2018年在美国菲奇堡建造了一架更大的纸飞机，但它没能飞起来。

1647
01:21:00.080 --> 01:21:00.600
Ah.
啊。

1648
01:21:01.360 --> 01:21:02.000
Yes.
是的。

1649
01:21:02.260 --> 01:21:07.640
And that concludes your paper airplane tidbits.
以上就是关于纸飞机的小知识。

1650
01:21:07.940 --> 01:21:09.000
I love them.
我喜欢这些。

1651
01:21:09.240 --> 01:21:10.400
Thank you very much.
非常感谢。

1652
01:21:10.640 --> 01:21:14.640
The next scene made me tear up and I was not expecting it.
接下来的那一幕让我热泪盈眶，我完全没料到会这样。

1653
01:21:14.640 --> 01:21:16.840
But I was sort of surprised.
但我确实有点惊讶。

1654
01:21:17.000 --> 01:21:19.100
I hadn't seen this episode since it aired.
自这集播出以来，我就没再看过它了。

1655
01:21:20.720 --> 01:21:24.280
And this whole Jim and Pam ending really got me, lady.
吉姆和帕姆的整个结局真的触动了我，女士。

1656
01:21:25.140 --> 01:21:28.540
You know, Jim is going to tell Pam that he's sorry that he has to go.
你知道，吉姆要告诉帕姆，他很抱歉不得不离开。

1657
01:21:28.780 --> 01:21:30.260
It's time for him to go back to Philly.
他该回费城了。

1658
01:21:30.680 --> 01:21:34.120
But he thinks they should keep working at this because they're making progress.
但他认为他们应该继续努力，因为他们正在取得进展。

1659
01:21:34.680 --> 01:21:37.940
And he kind of does that thing where he looks back, but she doesn't.
他做了那个回头看的动作，但她没有。

1660
01:21:38.000 --> 01:21:41.480
And then he leaves and then she looks towards the door, but he's already left.
然后他离开了，接着她看向门口，但他已经走了。

1661
01:21:41.760 --> 01:21:49.260
And then she sees that he left his umbrella and she hesitates for a second and decides to try to catch him to give it to him.
然后她看到他落下了雨伞，她犹豫了一秒，决定去追他把伞还给他。

1662
01:21:49.980 --> 01:21:57.360
Well, that scene at the desk where Jim comes really close to Pam, I remember when we were shooting this,
嗯，在办公桌前吉姆靠帕姆很近的那一幕，我记得我们拍摄的时候，

1663
01:21:57.480 --> 01:22:04.180
that this is the first time that our characters had been in one another's intimate personal space in a really long time.
那是我们的角色在很长一段时间里第一次进入彼此的亲密私人空间。

1664
01:22:04.500 --> 01:22:04.740
Yeah.
是的。

1665
01:22:04.960 --> 01:22:11.160
And not only was he in her sort of close proximity, but he was gentle.
他不仅靠近了她，而且很温柔。

1666
01:22:11.440 --> 01:22:12.380
He kneeled down.
他跪了下来。

1667
01:22:12.580 --> 01:22:13.520
He was next to her.
他在她身边。

1668
01:22:13.660 --> 01:22:14.680
He was being earneSt.
他表现得很真诚。

1669
01:22:14.680 --> 01:22:20.680
There was a connection between the two of them in that moment that we haven't seen in many episodes.
那一刻他们两人之间产生了一种我们在很多集里都没见过的联系。

1670
01:22:20.960 --> 01:22:22.500
He was being Jim.
他表现得就像吉姆。

1671
01:22:22.880 --> 01:22:23.200
Yeah.
是的。

1672
01:22:23.380 --> 01:22:24.800
He was being old Jim.
他表现得就像以前的吉姆。

1673
01:22:25.060 --> 01:22:27.480
All of the posturing of athlete was gone.
运动员的所有姿态都消失了。

1674
01:22:27.700 --> 01:22:32.040
And he was being the guy that she fell in love with.
他变回了那个她爱上的男人。

1675
01:22:32.220 --> 01:22:32.720
That's right.
没错。

1676
01:22:32.920 --> 01:22:34.880
And it was very moving to me.
这让我非常感动。

1677
01:22:35.060 --> 01:22:43.740
And it was hard for me to not kind of melt in that moment as Pam, you know, because she's wanted this for a really long time.
作为帕姆，那一刻我很难不融化，你知道，因为她渴望这一刻已经很久了。

1678
01:22:43.740 --> 01:22:46.680
So this was a really fun scene to play.
所以这一幕演起来非常有趣。

1679
01:22:46.900 --> 01:22:48.080
It had a lot of levels.
它有很多层次。

1680
01:22:48.500 --> 01:22:51.440
And then it leads to the scene in the parking lot.
然后它引出了停车场的那一幕。

1681
01:22:51.660 --> 01:22:54.560
Pam decides to run out and give Jim his umbrella.
帕姆决定跑出去把雨伞给吉姆。

1682
01:22:54.860 --> 01:22:56.520
And he hugs her.
然后他拥抱了她。

1683
01:22:56.740 --> 01:22:58.360
And I wrote this to you, Jenna.
我给你写过这个，珍娜。

1684
01:22:58.480 --> 01:22:59.440
We were trading texts.
我们当时在发短信。

1685
01:22:59.660 --> 01:23:04.400
I said, Jim hugs Pam like she's the last life preserver on the Titanic.
我说，吉姆拥抱帕姆的样子，就像她是泰坦尼克号上最后一个救生圈。

1686
01:23:04.700 --> 01:23:05.400
I know.
我知道。

1687
01:23:05.400 --> 01:23:07.020
He grabbed onto her.
他紧紧抓住了她。

1688
01:23:07.220 --> 01:23:08.000
He does.
他确实是。

1689
01:23:08.140 --> 01:23:10.500
And this is just such a beautiful scene.
这一幕真是太美了。

1690
01:23:10.500 --> 01:23:12.260
Pam is resistant at firSt.
帕姆起初是抗拒的。

1691
01:23:12.380 --> 01:23:17.460
And he just will not let her go until she breaks down that wall.
但他就是不肯放手，直到她打破了那道墙。

1692
01:23:17.460 --> 01:23:18.940
And she hugs him back.
然后她回抱了他。

1693
01:23:19.060 --> 01:23:20.120
And they kiss.
他们亲吻了。

1694
01:23:20.260 --> 01:23:21.460
And they say, I love you.
他们说，我爱你。

1695
01:23:21.680 --> 01:23:22.600
I teared up.
我流泪了。

1696
01:23:22.820 --> 01:23:23.620
I know.
我知道。

1697
01:23:23.740 --> 01:23:28.680
And they have this flashback to their wedding of Jim's brother, you know, reading from Corinthians.
他们还穿插了吉姆哥哥婚礼上的闪回镜头，你知道，就是读《哥林多前书》那段。

1698
01:23:29.020 --> 01:23:31.000
And, you know, that footage didn't exiSt.
而且，你知道，那些素材原本是不存在的。

1699
01:23:31.440 --> 01:23:35.380
We had to bring Blake Robbins in and set up the church.
我们不得不请来布莱克·罗宾斯，并布置了教堂。

1700
01:23:35.380 --> 01:23:38.300
Just that one corner of the church.
就只是教堂的那一个角落。

1701
01:23:38.660 --> 01:23:40.100
And he had to do that reading.
他必须得读那段台词。

1702
01:23:40.100 --> 01:23:41.980
We shot that just for this episode.
我们专门为这一集拍了那个镜头。

1703
01:23:42.180 --> 01:23:45.380
All the other footage was footage that we already had from that episode.
其余所有素材都是我们之前那一集里现有的。

1704
01:23:45.600 --> 01:23:46.920
But this was really beautiful.
但这部分真的很美。

1705
01:23:47.240 --> 01:23:49.160
You know, we had a fan question from Marie R.
你知道，我们收到了一位来自内布拉斯加州奥马哈市的粉丝Marie R.的提问，她说，

1706
01:23:49.280 --> 01:23:50.840
in Omaha, Nebraska, who said,
她说，

1707
01:23:51.600 --> 01:23:54.900
In the last scene where Jim and Pam hug and then kiss and remember their wedding,
在最后一幕里，吉姆和帕姆拥抱然后亲吻，回想起他们的婚礼时，

1708
01:23:55.460 --> 01:24:00.420
I noticed that it was in the parking lot where Jim first professed his love for Pam on casino night.
我注意到那是在停车场，也就是吉姆在赌场之夜第一次向帕姆表白的地方。

1709
01:24:00.420 --> 01:24:02.800
Was this intentional or just a coincidence?
这是刻意安排的还是纯属巧合？

1710
01:24:03.680 --> 01:24:05.420
Marie, this was intentional.
Marie，这是刻意安排的。

1711
01:24:06.660 --> 01:24:07.480
It's there.
就在那里。

1712
01:24:07.680 --> 01:24:09.320
It's happening in the same spot.
事情就发生在同一个地点。

1713
01:24:09.480 --> 01:24:12.840
This is such a wonderful bookends for their story.
这对他们的故事来说是一个非常美妙的呼应。

1714
01:24:13.420 --> 01:24:16.740
Kind of the first moment that Jim said, I'm in love with you.
算是吉姆第一次说“我爱你”的那个时刻。

1715
01:24:16.920 --> 01:24:20.020
And then here in the parking lot again to save the marriage.
然后又回到这个停车场，为了挽救他们的婚姻。

1716
01:24:20.200 --> 01:24:21.680
Just really beautiful writing.
编剧写得真是太棒了。

1717
01:24:22.200 --> 01:24:22.360
Yeah.
没错。

1718
01:24:22.960 --> 01:24:24.960
And we talked about this too, Angela.
安吉拉，我们也聊过这个。

1719
01:24:24.960 --> 01:24:32.200
You see in that moment the way John Krasinski as Jim swoops down to get to Pam's level for that hug.
在那一刻，你看到约翰·卡拉辛斯基饰演的吉姆俯下身去配合帕姆的身高进行拥抱。

1720
01:24:32.420 --> 01:24:35.540
That is a classic John Krasinski hugging move.
那是约翰·卡拉辛斯基标志性的拥抱动作。

1721
01:24:35.840 --> 01:24:37.740
We've talked about this before.
我们之前聊过这个。

1722
01:24:37.740 --> 01:24:39.540
He gives the best hugs.
他拥抱的感觉最好。

1723
01:24:39.820 --> 01:24:41.120
He gives such great hugs.
他给的拥抱太棒了。

1724
01:24:41.400 --> 01:24:46.280
He is just like that cozy blanket that makes you feel better.
他就好比那条让你感到安心的舒适毛毯。

1725
01:24:46.640 --> 01:24:47.300
I know.
我知道。

1726
01:24:47.440 --> 01:24:52.940
I just love now that he's a dad and has little girls because I know he hugs them like that.
我现在一想到他当了爸爸，有了小女儿，就觉得很开心，因为我知道他肯定也是这样拥抱她们的。

1727
01:24:52.940 --> 01:24:56.940
You know, I'm like, oh, that's the hug you want.
你知道，我就在想，噢，那就是你想要的拥抱。

1728
01:24:57.100 --> 01:24:59.900
That's the hug that makes everything feel like it's going to be okay.
那种能让你觉得一切都会好起来的拥抱。

1729
01:25:00.540 --> 01:25:00.900
Yes.
是的。

1730
01:25:01.020 --> 01:25:02.400
And it is that kind of hug.
确实是那种拥抱。

1731
01:25:02.500 --> 01:25:06.980
When he gives you a hug, it is like, oh my gosh, what was that bad day that I was having?
当他给你一个拥抱时，你会觉得，天哪，我刚才经历的糟糕一天算什么呢？

1732
01:25:07.540 --> 01:25:08.760
Everything's going to be fine.
一切都会好起来的。

1733
01:25:10.400 --> 01:25:12.740
And that's how the episode ends, everybody.
大家，这一集就是这样结束的。

1734
01:25:13.120 --> 01:25:16.300
I mean, we have a lot of thank yous for this one.
我是说，这一集我们要感谢的人有很多。

1735
01:25:16.440 --> 01:25:17.980
It was such a joy to rewatch.
重温这一集真是太开心了。

1736
01:25:17.980 --> 01:25:22.940
Thanks again to Steve Burgess for the call sheets and answering our questions.
再次感谢史蒂夫·伯吉斯提供的拍摄通告单并回答我们的问题。

1737
01:25:23.320 --> 01:25:26.720
You know, I really loved hearing from Warren and Halstead on this.
你知道，我真的很喜欢听沃伦和霍尔斯特德分享关于这一集的内容。

1738
01:25:26.900 --> 01:25:36.380
One of the things they shared that I wanted to mention but forgot in the moment was they said they loved writing for Daryl and Andy for that friendship.
他们分享的一件事我当时想提却忘了，就是他们说很喜欢为达里尔和安迪写那段友谊的戏份。

1739
01:25:36.740 --> 01:25:37.000
Yeah.
没错。

1740
01:25:37.000 --> 01:25:39.060
And you really see it in this.
你在这一集里真的能看出来。

1741
01:25:39.200 --> 01:25:48.100
I didn't bring it up, but I loved the pep talk that Daryl gave Andy when he said, Andy Bernard can't squirt water in his eye and act like it doesn't freak him out.
我没提过，但我很喜欢达里尔给安迪打气时说的话，他说：“安迪·伯纳德不能被水喷到眼睛还装作若无其事。”

1742
01:25:48.180 --> 01:25:48.960
But you know who can?
但你知道谁可以吗？

1743
01:25:49.280 --> 01:25:51.440
Older male lab assistant number one.
一号年长男性实验助理。

1744
01:25:51.740 --> 01:25:52.220
Yes.
没错。

1745
01:25:52.500 --> 01:25:55.140
And Andy says, do you believe in me?
然后安迪说：“你相信我吗？”

1746
01:25:55.240 --> 01:25:58.480
And Daryl says, I believe I want to go home.
达里尔说：“我相信我想回家了。”

1747
01:25:59.020 --> 01:25:59.320
Yeah.
哈哈。

1748
01:25:59.820 --> 01:26:00.540
That was so good.
那段太精彩了。

1749
01:26:00.540 --> 01:26:03.900
Anyway, Warren and Halstead just said they loved writing for those two.
总之，沃伦和霍尔斯特德就是说他们很喜欢为这两个角色写戏。

1750
01:26:04.100 --> 01:26:09.400
And thank you, Warren and Halstead, for sharing everything you did about all the different storylines and the behind-the-scenes details.
也谢谢沃伦和霍尔斯特德，感谢你们分享了关于所有不同剧情线和幕后细节的一切。

1751
01:26:09.840 --> 01:26:14.360
I also want to thank my friend Pete Holney for sending in his audio clip.
我也要感谢我的朋友皮特·霍尔尼发来他的音频片段。

1752
01:26:14.520 --> 01:26:15.860
I love his stories.
我喜欢他的故事。

1753
01:26:16.300 --> 01:26:18.040
And I wanted to give a shout-out.
我还想特别提一下。

1754
01:26:18.180 --> 01:26:22.380
Pete said that him and his brother, you know, they were the twin elves in Elf.
皮特说他和他的兄弟，你知道的，他们是电影《精灵总动员》里的那对双胞胎精灵。

1755
01:26:22.440 --> 01:26:22.640
Yep.
没错。

1756
01:26:23.320 --> 01:26:25.500
They do Christmas parties, lady.
女士，他们会承接圣诞派对。

1757
01:26:25.760 --> 01:26:27.460
And corporate hootenannies.
还有公司联欢会。

1758
01:26:27.460 --> 01:26:32.180
And I'll share in stories, if you want the two twin elves from Elf, they'll come to your party.
我会分享这些故事，如果你想要《精灵总动员》里的那对双胞胎精灵来参加你的派对，他们会去的。

1759
01:26:32.640 --> 01:26:34.300
That is so fun.
那太有趣了。

1760
01:26:34.560 --> 01:26:35.120
I know.
我知道。

1761
01:26:35.180 --> 01:26:35.720
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1762
01:26:36.260 --> 01:26:36.880
They have the costumes and everything.
他们有服装还有各种装备。

1763
01:26:37.140 --> 01:26:38.060
What a good idea.
真是个好主意。

1764
01:26:38.300 --> 01:26:44.640
Well, I want to give a shout-out to Halstead, who's got two exciting projects coming up I think everyone should be on the lookout for.
嗯，我想特别提一下霍尔斯特德，他有两个令人兴奋的项目即将推出，我认为每个人都应该关注一下。

1765
01:26:44.640 --> 01:26:51.340
The first is How to Die Alone, starring Natasha Rothwell, which will premiere on Hulu on September 13th.
第一个是娜塔莎·罗斯韦尔主演的《如何孤独死去》，将于9月13日在Hulu首播。

1766
01:26:51.340 --> 01:26:58.240
And the other is a college comedy called Overcompensating, and it's starring Benito Skinner, a.k.a.
另一个是名为《过度补偿》的大学喜剧，由Instagram上的贝尼托·斯金纳，也就是贝尼·德拉马主演。

1767
01:26:58.380 --> 01:26:59.740
Benny Drama, from Instagram.
贝尼·德拉马，来自Instagram。

1768
01:26:59.920 --> 01:27:02.720
And that will premiere on Amazon sometime next year.
该剧将于明年某个时候在亚马逊首播。

1769
01:27:03.200 --> 01:27:04.240
Well, there you go.
好了，就是这样。

1770
01:27:04.480 --> 01:27:07.160
Thank you guys so much for sending in your questions and comments.
非常感谢大家发来你们的问题和评论。

1771
01:27:07.300 --> 01:27:07.740
We love you.
我们爱你们。

1772
01:27:08.180 --> 01:27:15.760
Big thank you to Jenna and Cassie and Sean for recording on a Saturday morning so I can go do this fun project I can't wait to share about.
非常感谢珍娜、卡西和肖恩在周六早上录音，这样我就可以去参加这个我迫不及待想分享的有趣项目了。

1773
01:27:15.760 --> 01:27:17.000
Yeah, of course.
当然可以。

1774
01:27:17.240 --> 01:27:20.660
And when we're back together, we should do a paper airplane conteSt.
等我们再聚在一起时，我们应该举办一场纸飞机比赛。

1775
01:27:21.340 --> 01:27:21.880
Yes!
好啊！

1776
01:27:22.900 --> 01:27:23.900
Let's do it.
就这么定了。

1777
01:27:23.900 --> 01:27:25.860
But we have to fold them ourselves, Cassie.
但我们必须自己折，卡西。

1778
01:27:26.000 --> 01:27:27.720
We can't get any pros coming in.
我们不能请专业人士来。

1779
01:27:28.000 --> 01:27:29.620
I'll get the rules, okay?
我去制定规则，好吗？

1780
01:27:29.880 --> 01:27:30.220
Okay.
好的。

1781
01:27:30.800 --> 01:27:31.460
All right, everyone.
好了，各位。

1782
01:27:31.460 --> 01:27:32.280
Have a great week.
祝大家度过愉快的一周。

1783
01:27:32.600 --> 01:27:33.680
See you next time.
下次见。

1784
01:27:41.400 --> 01:27:43.480
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1785
01:27:43.800 --> 01:27:49.000
Office Ladies is a presentation of Odyssey and is produced by Jenna Fisher and Angela Kinsey.
《办公室女士》由Odyssey出品，由珍娜·费舍尔和安吉拉·金赛制作。

1786
01:27:49.200 --> 01:27:51.580
Our executive producer is Cassie Jerkins.
我们的执行制片人是卡西·杰金斯。

1787
01:27:51.580 --> 01:27:56.400
Our audio engineer is Sam Kiefer and our associate producer is Ainsley Bubbico.
我们的音频工程师是萨姆·基弗，助理制片人是安斯利·布比科。

1788
01:27:56.940 --> 01:28:01.180
Odyssey's executive producers are Jenna Weiss-Berman and Leah Reese-Dennis.
Odyssey的执行制片人是珍娜·韦斯-伯曼和莉亚·里斯-丹尼斯。

1789
01:28:01.640 --> 01:28:04.120
Office Ladies is mixed and mastered by Chris Basil.
《办公室女士》由克里斯·巴兹尔混音和母带处理。

1790
01:28:04.620 --> 01:28:07.240
Our theme song is Rubber Tree by Creed Bratton.
我们的主题曲是克里德·布拉顿演唱的《橡胶树》。
